P1498="matrix/tactics/TA0040-impact/techniques/NJT-0198-network-denial-of-service"
write(f"{P1498}/technique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"technique","id":"NJT-0198","name":B("网络拒绝服务","Network Denial of Service"),"summary":B("攻击者以汇聚攻击流量耗尽网络路径或边界容量，并通过来源分布或响应来源置换提高局部检测与归因成本。","Adversaries aggregate attack traffic to exhaust network-path or boundary capacity while source distribution or response-origin displacement raises local detection and attribution cost."),"aliases":["T1498"],"classification":{"tactic_refs":["TA0040"],"origin":{"kind":"attack-adapted","source_attack_id":"T1498","source_attack_version":"19.1"},"decision_ref":"DEC-TA0040-T1498"},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("网络拒绝服务是攻击者让链路、边界设备、网络协议或面向网络的容量无法承载合法通信，使用户虽可能面对仍存活的端点，却无法建立或维持预期连接。直接对象是网络路径及汇聚容量，而不是端点内部线程、应用资源或攻击者用带宽完成的代理/挖矿任务。","Network Denial of Service prevents a link, boundary device, network protocol, or network-facing capacity from carrying legitimate communication, so users cannot establish or maintain expected connections even if endpoints remain alive. The direct object is network path and aggregate capacity, not internal endpoint workers or application resources or attacker bandwidth used for proxying or mining."),("Niji 关注来源拓扑怎样让完整攻击在任何单源/单域中难以识别，以及反射怎样让可见响应来源替代真实发起者。直接高流量洪泛保持父级核心；协议、放大倍数、botnet 家族和目标端口是实现。","Niji focuses on source topology that keeps the complete attack from appearing in one origin or domain and reflection that makes visible responders replace the true initiator. Direct high-volume flooding remains parent core; protocol, amplification ratio, botnet family, and target port are implementations.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("多源洪泛把总量拆到大量真实来源，每源贡献可接近普通用户，源侧与短窗规则只见低强度事件，目的或中转处才形成容量损失。响应源置换则用受害者伪造源驱动合法第三方回包，使受害侧记录的是 DNS/NTP/其他服务响应者，而不是发送诱导请求的攻击者。","Multi-source flooding divides total volume across many real origins so each contribution can resemble an ordinary user, leaving origin-side and short-window rules with weak events while destination or transit suffers capacity loss. Response-origin displacement spoofs the victim source to drive legitimate third-party replies, so victim-side records show DNS, NTP, or other responders rather than the attacker that sent inducement requests."),("残余包括 IPFIX 流、来源/AS 分布、目的 fan-in、包字节比、接口 octet/packet/discard、容量利用、无对应请求的响应和上游清洗结果。flash crowds、软件发布、灾难新闻和合法大响应可形成相似汇聚，需业务/协议基线排除。","Residue includes IPFIX flow, source and AS distribution, destination fan-in, packet-to-byte ratio, interface octet, packet and discard counters, capacity utilization, responses without matching requests, and upstream scrubbing outcome. Flash crowds, software releases, disaster news, and legitimate large responses can create similar aggregation and need business and protocol baselines.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入攻击流量与网络容量/丢弃/时延、合法通信失败之间的因果。高流量但容量充足、被上游完全吸收、扫描或 botnet 心跳无合法通信影响时只为企图/相邻行为。","Include a causal relation among attack traffic, network capacity or discard or latency, and failed legitimate communication. High traffic with sufficient capacity, fully absorbed upstream, scanning, or botnet heartbeat without legitimate-communication impact is attempt or adjacent behavior."),("端点内部资源耗尽归 NJT-0199；为攻击者任务消费 victim bandwidth 归 NJT-0189；C2 与 botnet 建立是前置。反射器自身正常响应不等于其被攻陷，必须区分真实执行来源、可见来源和受害目的。","Endpoint-internal exhaustion belongs to NJT-0199, victim bandwidth consumed for attacker work to NJT-0189, and C2 or botnet establishment is precursor. A reflector responding normally is not necessarily compromised; distinguish real execution origin, visible origin, and victim destination.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("攻击者可协调大量 bot/代理向同一边界发送低到中等单源流量，或向开放解析器/放大服务发送伪造受害源请求，使第三方响应在目标链路汇聚。目的可能是政治中断、勒索或掩护其他活动。","An attacker can coordinate many bots or proxies to send low-to-moderate per-origin traffic to one boundary, or send victim-spoofed requests to open resolvers or amplifiers so third-party responses converge on the target link. Purposes include political disruption, extortion, or cover for other activity."),P("攻击者需要足够真实来源或可伪造源网络，以及对目标容量、协议反射面和汇聚路径的理解。源验证、反射服务访问控制、Anycast/CDN、上游清洗和速率/容量保护提高成本。","The attacker needs enough real origins or spoof-capable networks and knowledge of target capacity, protocol reflection surfaces, and convergence paths. Source validation, reflector access control, Anycast or CDN, upstream scrubbing, and rate or capacity protection raise cost."),P("防守方可观察 IPFIX/NetFlow、接口容量与丢弃、BGP/AS、DNS/NTP 等协议请求响应、边界健康、上游告警和业务可用性，并跨 observationDomain 聚合。采样、NAT/代理、加密和缺少 victim 出站请求日志会削弱来源与反射判断。","Defenders observe IPFIX or NetFlow, interface capacity and discard, BGP or AS, protocol request and response such as DNS or NTP, boundary health, upstream alerts, and business availability and aggregate across observation domains. Sampling, NAT or proxying, encryption, and missing victim outbound requests weaken source and reflection assessment.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-ST","primary",B("多源低贡献流量在目的端汇聚成容量损失","Low-contribution traffic from many sources converges into capacity loss"),P("攻击者把洪泛分散到大量真实来源，每个来源的事件强度下降，而目的端 fan-in 和链路利用累积。单源或单域短窗分析无法看到整体，跨来源长期聚合恢复，形成时空释痕。","The attacker disperses flooding across many real origins, lowering event strength per source while destination fan-in and link utilization accumulate. Per-source or single-domain short-window analysis misses the whole, while cross-source long-horizon aggregation restores it, producing spatiotemporal trace dilution."),["REF-000956","REF-000957","REF-000958"],"high"),mechanism("NM-FD","secondary",B("第三方响应者替代真实发起者成为受害侧可见来源","Third-party responders replace the real initiator as victim-visible sources"),P("攻击者伪造受害者地址向第三方服务发请求，响应者按协议回包。目标记录合法服务来源，真实发起者仅在诱导请求一侧留下痕迹，来源外观与因果错位形成特征伪装。","The attacker sends victim-spoofed requests to third-party services, which reply normally. The target records legitimate service origins while the true initiator appears only on the inducement side, producing feature disguise through origin-causality mismatch."),["REF-000956","REF-000958","REF-000960"],"high")],
"subtechnique_taxonomy":{"narrative":PP(("多源低贡献洪泛按真实执行来源分布划分，检测依赖跨来源 fan-in 与容量；响应源归因置换按可见响应者与真实发起者分离划分，检测依赖无对应请求和反射协议。二者可组合但防御不可互换。","Multi-Source Low-Contribution Flooding is divided by distribution of real executing origins and requires cross-source fan-in and capacity analysis. Response-Origin Displacement is divided by separation of visible responders from the true initiator and requires unmatched requests and reflection-protocol analysis. They can combine but defenses are not interchangeable."),("T1498.001/.002 只作直接与反射实现广度。单/少源直接洪泛和协议/放大倍数留父级，botnet 名称、端口和地理不形成 NJS。","T1498.001 and .002 remain implementation breadth for direct and reflected flooding. Single or few-source direct floods and protocol or amplification ratio remain parent core; botnet name, port, and geography do not define NJS.")),"coverage":"established","subtechnique_refs":["NJS-0198-001","NJS-0198-002"]},
"defense":defense(["DET-000230"],["MIT-000205"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000971","CLM-000972","CLM-000973","CLM-000974","CLM-000975","CLM-000976"],"case_refs":[],"reference_refs":["REF-000955","REF-000956","REF-000957","REF-000958","REF-000959","REF-000960","REF-000664","REF-000961","REF-000962","REF-000963","REF-000899"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("NIST/IETF 高置信支持分布式与反射拓扑、源伪造和控制，但没有为本批建立一个具完整受害链的命名 CASE。来源分布也可能为 flash crowd，反射响应者通常是被滥用而非被控制。","NIST and IETF strongly support distributed and reflection topology, spoofing, and controls, but this batch has no named CASE with a complete victim chain. Source distribution can also be a flash crowd, and reflectors are usually abused rather than controlled."),("流量采样与多域数据共享限制精确归因；任何固定 10 秒/60 秒阈值必须按链路容量、业务和采样调优。","Traffic sampling and cross-domain data sharing limit attribution; any fixed 10-second or 60-second threshold needs tuning to link capacity, business, and sampling."))},"lifecycle":life()})

write(f"{P1498}/subtechniques/NJS-0198-001-multi-source-low-contribution-flooding/subtechnique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"evasion-subtechnique","id":"NJS-0198-001","parent_ref":"NJT-0198","name":B("多源低贡献洪泛","Multi-Source Low-Contribution Flooding"),"summary":B("攻击者把洪泛分散到大量真实来源，使每源贡献低而目的端汇聚后耗尽容量。","An adversary distributes flooding across many real sources so each contributes little while destination aggregation exhausts capacity."),"aliases":[],"lineage":{"attck_subtechnique_inherited":False},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("多源低贡献洪泛通过多个真实执行来源协同向同一目的、前缀或服务发送互补流量，让单源速率/包量保持较低而聚合 fan-in 超过网络容量。稳定变量是真实来源分布与局部贡献，不是 botnet 家族、国家或协议。","Multi-Source Low-Contribution Flooding coordinates multiple real executing origins toward one destination, prefix, or service so per-source rate or packets stay low while aggregate fan-in exceeds network capacity. The stable variable is real-origin distribution and local contribution, not botnet family, country, or protocol."),("完成要求目的路径容量/丢弃和合法通信失败；多源扫描、C2 心跳或未饱和流量不是本项。来源数量本身无固定阈值，需相对于每源基线和总体容量判断。","Completion requires destination path capacity or discard and failed legitimate communication. Multi-source scanning, C2 heartbeat, or unsaturated traffic falls outside. Source count has no universal threshold and is judged against per-source baseline and aggregate capacity.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("多源低贡献洪泛使每个来源只留下接近普通连接的弱信号，攻击总量只在目的或中转汇聚。单源限速与一个 observation domain 无法看见完整图像；来源/AS 分布、目的 fan-in、容量和丢弃的跨域关联仍可恢复。","Multi-Source Low-Contribution Flooding leaves only weak ordinary-looking signals per origin while total attack appears at destination or transit aggregation. Per-source rate limits and one observation domain miss the full picture; cross-domain correlation of source or AS distribution, destination fan-in, capacity, and discard restores it.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入多个真实来源低局部贡献、同一目的聚合和网络可用性结果。单一 NAT 后大量合法用户、CDN、软件发布和自然 flash crowd 是反例；伪造同一受害源驱动第三方响应属于兄弟项。","Include low local contribution from multiple real origins, aggregation at one destination, and network-availability outcome. Many legitimate users behind NAT, CDN, software release, and natural flash crowd are counterexamples; third-party responses driven by a spoofed victim source belong to the sibling.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("攻击者控制 bot、代理或受侵主机群，让每节点发送不高的 UDP/TCP/HTTP 流量，目标边界在总体上被耗尽。","An attacker controls bots, proxies, or compromised hosts and has each send modest UDP, TCP, or HTTP traffic while aggregate traffic exhausts the target boundary."),P("攻击者需要足够来源、同步能力和目标容量知识，并承受节点失效与上游阻断；Anycast、CDN、清洗和跨源限额降低效果。","The attacker needs enough origins, coordination, and knowledge of target capacity and tolerates node loss and upstream blocking; Anycast, CDN, scrubbing, and cross-source limits reduce the effect."),P("防守方需要多域流量、目的容量、来源/AS 基线和合法业务事件。采样、共享限制和代理/NAT 会降低来源判断。","Defenders need multidomain flows, destination capacity, source or AS baselines, and legitimate business events. Sampling, sharing limits, and proxies or NAT weaken source assessment.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-ST","primary",B("每源低贡献在目的端聚合为容量耗尽","Low per-source contribution aggregates into destination capacity exhaustion"),P("攻击者把总洪泛拆散到来源与时间，局部事件低于单源门槛，目的 fan-in 和接口利用却累积。跨观察域聚合恢复完整活动。","The attacker divides total flooding across origins and time, keeping local events below per-source thresholds while destination fan-in and interface utilization accumulate. Cross-observation-domain aggregation restores the complete activity."),["REF-000956","REF-000957","REF-000958"],"high")],
"defense":defense(["DET-000230"],["MIT-000205"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000972","CLM-000974","CLM-000976"],"case_refs":[],"reference_refs":["REF-000956","REF-000957","REF-000958","REF-000664","REF-000961","REF-000962"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("标准与研究支持来源拓扑与汇聚效果，但来源数量、单源贡献和饱和阈值随链路/采样变化；无命名 CASE。","Standards and research support source topology and aggregation effects, but source count, local contribution, and saturation thresholds vary by link and sampling; no named CASE is used."),("flash crowd 与大型合法事件可能完全同形，需 owner、事件日历和协议行为排除。","Flash crowds and large legitimate events can be isomorphic and require owner, event-calendar, and protocol behavior for exclusion."))},"lifecycle":life()})

write(f"{P1498}/subtechniques/NJS-0198-002-response-origin-displacement/subtechnique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"evasion-subtechnique","id":"NJS-0198-002","parent_ref":"NJT-0198","name":B("响应源归因置换","Response-Origin Displacement"),"summary":B("攻击者伪造受害源驱动第三方服务回包，使合法响应者成为受害侧可见来源并隐藏真实发起者。","An adversary spoofs the victim source to drive third-party replies, making legitimate responders victim-visible origins and hiding the true initiator."),"aliases":[],"lineage":{"attck_subtechnique_inherited":False},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("响应源归因置换是攻击者以受害者地址为源向第三方 UDP/无连接服务发送请求，使这些服务向受害者产生响应流量。稳定变量是可见响应来源与真实诱导请求发起者分离；是否放大、协议名称和 reflector 数量是实现。","Response-Origin Displacement sends requests to third-party UDP or connectionless services with the victim address as source so those services reply to the victim. The stable variable is separation of visible response origin from the true inducement requester; amplification, protocol name, and reflector count are implementations."),("完成要求无对应 victim 请求、第三方响应与容量损失相连。正常递归、缓存、异步 webhook 或合法服务回包不是本项。","Completion requires absent corresponding victim requests and third-party responses joined to capacity loss. Normal recursion, caching, asynchronous webhooks, or legitimate service replies are excluded.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("响应源归因置换让目标看到大量真实 DNS/NTP/其他服务地址，黑名单和受害侧来源调查指向被滥用响应者，而真实攻击者在另一网络发送小请求。请求—响应不对称、协议事务 ID、包长比和无出站请求仍可揭示因果。","Response-Origin Displacement makes the target see real DNS, NTP, or other service addresses, directing blacklists and victim-side source investigation toward abused responders while the attacker sends small requests elsewhere. Request-response asymmetry, protocol transaction IDs, packet-size ratio, and absent outbound requests reveal causality.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入伪造 victim source、第三方协议响应、无对应请求和网络容量/通信失败的链。直接 bot 流量、被攻陷 reflector 上的攻击代码或仅源地址欺骗而无反射结果不满足。","Include a chain of spoofed victim source, third-party protocol responses, no corresponding request, and network capacity or communication failure. Direct bot traffic, attack code on a compromised reflector, or source spoofing without a reflection outcome do not qualify.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("攻击者向开放 DNS 递归器、NTP 或其他反射服务发送小请求并伪造 victim 地址，第三方响应在目标汇聚。","An attacker sends small requests to open DNS resolvers, NTP, or other reflectors with the victim address spoofed, and third-party responses converge on the target."),P("攻击者需要可伪造源的网络与可访问 reflector；BCP38、服务 ACL 和响应限速限制效果。","The attacker needs a spoof-capable network and reachable reflectors; BCP38, service ACLs, and response limiting constrain it."),P("防守方要连接 victim 出站请求、入站响应、协议字段、来源 AS 和容量；没有出站日志时只能概率判断。","Defenders join victim outbound requests, inbound responses, protocol fields, source AS, and capacity; without outbound logs only probabilistic classification is possible.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-FD","primary",B("合法第三方响应者掩盖诱导请求发起者","Legitimate third-party responders disguise the inducement requester"),P("攻击者伪造受害源，第三方按协议响应，受害侧来源身份被置换为正常服务。真实攻击者与大流量不在同一观察面，形成特征伪装；无请求响应关联恢复。","The attacker spoofs the victim source and third parties reply normally, replacing victim-visible origin identity with legitimate services. The real attacker and large traffic are in different observation planes, producing feature disguise; unmatched-response correlation restores it."),["REF-000956","REF-000958","REF-000960"],"high")],
"defense":defense(["DET-000230"],["MIT-000205"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000973","CLM-000975","CLM-000976"],"case_refs":[],"reference_refs":["REF-000956","REF-000958","REF-000959","REF-000960","REF-000664"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("规范资料高置信支持反射因果，但不同协议的请求/响应字段和放大语义不可互换；无命名 CASE。","Normative sources strongly support reflection causality, but request and response fields and amplification semantics are not interchangeable across protocols; no named CASE is used."),("缺 victim 出站日志、NAT/Anycast 和采样会削弱无请求判断；合法异步响应需协议/业务基线。","Missing victim outbound logs, NAT or Anycast, and sampling weaken unmatched-response analysis; legitimate asynchronous responses need protocol and business baselines."))},"lifecycle":life()})

P1499="matrix/tactics/TA0040-impact/techniques/NJT-0199-endpoint-denial-of-service"
write(f"{P1499}/technique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"technique","id":"NJT-0199","name":B("端点拒绝服务","Endpoint Denial of Service"),"summary":B("攻击者使端点内部资源耗尽或触发故障，并用低速状态保持或输入成本放大削弱失效前兆。","Adversaries exhaust endpoint-internal resources or trigger faults while low-rate state holding or input-cost amplification weakens failure precursors."),"aliases":["T1499"],"classification":{"tactic_refs":["TA0040"],"origin":{"kind":"attack-adapted","source_attack_id":"T1499","source_attack_version":"19.1"},"decision_ref":"DEC-TA0040-T1499"},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("端点拒绝服务是攻击者使主机、操作系统、服务进程或应用因连接/会话、线程、队列、句柄、CPU、内存、事件循环或缺陷触发而不能为合法用户提供预期功能。直接对象是端点内部可用性；网络地址仍可达或进程仍存活，不否定服务挂起或无工作槽位。","Endpoint Denial of Service makes a host, OS, service process, or application unable to serve legitimate users because connection or session state, workers, queues, handles, CPU, memory, event loop, or a triggered flaw is exhausted or blocked. The direct object is endpoint-internal availability; a reachable address or surviving process does not negate a hang or absence of worker slots."),("Niji 关注外部输入量与内部损失如何脱钩：低速请求长期持有状态，或少量输入触发不成比例计算/故障。高流量普通耗尽留父级；栈层、漏洞编号和平台是实现。","Niji focuses on decoupling external input volume from internal loss: slow requests hold state for long periods, or small inputs trigger disproportionate computation or fault. Ordinary high-volume exhaustion remains parent core; stack layer, vulnerability ID, and platform are implementations.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("状态保持攻击以低数据率让连接、头部、请求体或会话长期未完成，带宽和单源速率低但并发状态积累。成本放大用少量正常外形输入触发指数回溯或昂贵解析，使内部 CPU/事件循环/内存远高于输入量。请求量 alone 会低估两者。","State-holding attacks use low data rates to keep connections, headers, bodies, or sessions incomplete, with low bandwidth and per-source rate but accumulating concurrency. Cost amplification uses a few normal-looking inputs to trigger exponential backtracking or expensive parsing, making internal CPU, event-loop, or memory cost far exceed input. Request count alone underestimates both."),("残余包括活动/完成连接比、连接年龄和字节进度、工作线程/句柄/队列、每请求时延和长度、路由、错误、CPU/内存、OOM/崩溃/重启和外部健康。无入口—内部资源—健康关联时，故障容易被归因于容量或代码回归。","Residue includes active-to-completed connection ratio, age and byte progress, workers, handles, queues, per-request duration and length, route, errors, CPU or memory, OOM, crash or restart, and external health. Without ingress-to-internal-resource-to-health joins, failures can be attributed to capacity or regression.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入攻击输入与端点内部耗尽/故障之间可验证因果及实际合法功能损失。资源升高但健康正常、被限流无影响、失败探测和非关键进程崩溃为企图/相邻；正常峰值、慢客户端、大上传、缓存冷启、GC 和配置不足是反例。","Include verified causality from adversary input to internal exhaustion or fault and actual legitimate-function loss. Raised resources with healthy service, rate-limited no-impact traffic, failed probes, and noncritical crashes are attempts or adjacent; normal peaks, slow clients, large uploads, cold cache, GC, and insufficient capacity are counterexamples."),("有序管理停止归 NJT-0185，网络路径容量归 NJT-0198，为攻击者任务消费资源归 NJT-0189。漏洞利用需另证执行/权限结果；自动恢复不否定短暂 DoS，但需记录持续时间和用户范围。","Orderly management stop belongs to NJT-0185, network-path capacity to NJT-0198, and resource use for adversary work to NJT-0189. Exploitation needs separate execution or privilege evidence. Automatic recovery does not negate transient DoS but duration and user scope must be recorded.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("Web 端点可被大量低进度连接占用工作池，而接入带宽未饱和；或攻击者向低效正则/解析路径提交短输入，阻塞事件循环或少数工作线程。系统服务和内核也可出现低输入、高内部代价。","A web endpoint can have its worker pool occupied by many low-progress connections while ingress bandwidth remains unsaturated, or receive short crafted input on an inefficient regex or parser path that blocks an event loop or workers. System services and kernels can show the same low-input, high-internal-cost relation."),P("状态保持攻击者需维持会话并围绕 timeout/min-rate 发送；成本放大攻击者需发现高复杂度/故障输入。超时、限额、非回溯算法、输入界限、隔离池和故障转移限制效果。","A state-holder maintains sessions and sends around timeout or minimum-rate bounds; a cost amplifier finds high-complexity or faulting input. Timeouts, limits, nonbacktracking algorithms, input bounds, isolated pools, and failover constrain it."),P("防守方观察负载均衡连接/请求/字节/拒绝、未完成状态、Web 日志、工作池、OTel 路由/时延/错误、进程资源、崩溃和外部健康。完成日志会漏持有状态，源 IP 阈值会漏多源低速，只有主机资源无法区分代码回归。","Defenders observe load-balancer connections, requests, bytes and rejects, incomplete state, Web logs, worker pools, OTel route, duration and error, process resource, crash, and external health. Completion logs miss held state, source-IP thresholds miss distributed slow activity, and host resource alone cannot separate regression.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-ST","primary",B("低进度连接跨时间累积并发状态","Low-progress connections accumulate concurrent state over time"),P("攻击者把请求拆成低速进度并维持未完成状态，流量在时间和来源上稀释而连接槽持续占用。短窗流量无法还原累计耗尽，连接年龄、进度和全局并发可恢复。","The attacker fragments requests into low-rate progress and maintains incomplete state, diluting traffic across time and sources while slots remain occupied. Short-window volume misses accumulated exhaustion, while age, progress, and global concurrency restore it."),["REF-000965","REF-000966","REF-000967"],"high"),mechanism("NM-FD","secondary",B("小型请求外观掩盖不成比例的内部工作","Small request appearance disguises disproportionate internal work"),P("短输入触发回溯或高复杂度路径，外部数量/长度接近正常而内部工作异常增长。入口外观不表明代价，形成特征伪装；每请求时延、输入结构和健康结果揭示。","Short input triggers backtracking or high-complexity paths; external count and length resemble normal while internal work grows abnormally. Ingress appearance does not reveal cost, producing feature disguise; per-request duration, input structure, and health expose it."),["REF-000968","REF-000969","REF-000970"],"high")],
"subtechnique_taxonomy":{"narrative":PP(("状态保持式低速耗尽按进度率与持有时长积累并发状态划分；输入到工作量成本放大按输入复杂度与内部工作不对称划分。前者单事务工作低/持有长，后者单事务代价高/输入小，检测不可互换。","State-Holding Low-Rate Exhaustion is divided by progress rate and holding duration accumulating state; Input-to-Work Cost Amplification by asymmetry between input complexity and internal work. The former has low per-transaction work and long hold, the latter high per-transaction cost and small input, requiring different detection."),("T1499.001–.004 仅作 OS/服务/应用/利用广度，不导入。普通高量耗尽留父级，来源分布与 crash 外观证据不足而 defer。","T1499.001–.004 remain OS, service, application, and exploit breadth only and are not imported. Ordinary high-volume exhaustion remains parent core; source distribution and crash appearance remain deferred.")),"coverage":"established","subtechnique_refs":["NJS-0199-001","NJS-0199-002"]},
"defense":defense(["DET-000231"],["MIT-000206"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000977","CLM-000978","CLM-000979","CLM-000980","CLM-000981","CLM-000982"],"case_refs":[],"reference_refs":["REF-000964","REF-000965","REF-000966","REF-000967","REF-000968","REF-000969","REF-000970","REF-000971","REF-000972","REF-000973","REF-000974","REF-000975","REF-000976"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("权威技术文档高置信支持慢 HTTP 和 ReDoS，跨协议、解析器和内核泛化为中等。无命名在野 CASE，不能从高时延 alone 推断攻击。","Authoritative technical sources strongly support slow HTTP and ReDoS; generalization across protocols, parsers, and kernels is medium. There is no named field CASE and high latency alone cannot infer attack."),("正常慢客户端、流量峰值和代码回归需要入口、内部资源及外部健康三面关联排除；窗口和阈值需按服务调优。","Normal slow clients, traffic peaks, and regressions require ingress, internal-resource, and external-health joins; windows and thresholds require service tuning."))},"lifecycle":life()})

write(f"{P1499}/subtechniques/NJS-0199-001-state-holding-low-rate-exhaustion/subtechnique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"evasion-subtechnique","id":"NJS-0199-001","parent_ref":"NJT-0199","name":B("状态保持式低速耗尽","State-Holding Low-Rate Exhaustion"),"summary":B("攻击者以低进度维持大量未完成连接或事务，使并发状态累积而流量仍低。","An adversary maintains many incomplete connections or transactions with low progress so concurrent state accumulates while traffic stays low."),"aliases":[],"lineage":{"attck_subtechnique_inherited":False},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("状态保持式低速耗尽通过控制请求阶段、字节进度和持有时间，让连接、header/body、会话或工作槽长期未完成，直至内部并发资源耗尽。稳定变量是低进度与长持有，不是 HTTP 工具或来源数量。","State-Holding Low-Rate Exhaustion controls request stage, byte progress, and holding time so connections, headers or bodies, sessions, or worker slots remain incomplete until internal concurrency is exhausted. The stable variable is low progress and long holding, not an HTTP tool or source count.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("状态保持式低速耗尽让每连接带宽和单源请求率低，完成请求日志甚至无记录，短窗阈值低估正在占槽的状态。连接年龄、progress、活动/完成比、timeout 和池容量仍可见。","State-Holding Low-Rate Exhaustion keeps per-connection bandwidth and source request rate low; completion logs may contain no record and short windows underestimate occupied state. Connection age, progress, active-to-completed ratio, timeouts, and pool capacity remain visible.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入大量低进度未完成事务与池/连接状态耗尽及合法请求失败。正常慢网络、大上传、长轮询和批准持久连接是反例；完成的小输入高工作归兄弟项。","Include many low-progress incomplete transactions joined to pool or connection-state exhaustion and failed legitimate requests. Slow networks, large uploads, long polling, and approved persistent connections are counterexamples; completed small inputs causing high work belong to the sibling.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("攻击者维持慢 header/body 或 keepalive，使 Web 服务器连接/worker 长期占用。","An attacker maintains slow headers, bodies, or keepalives so Web server connections or workers stay occupied."),P("攻击者需足够会话并绕过 timeout/min-rate，可能多源分布；代理超时、并发限额和最小速率限制效果。","The attacker needs enough sessions and to evade timeout or minimum rate, possibly with many sources; proxy timeouts, concurrency limits, and minimum rates constrain it."),P("防守方保留未完成连接、age/progress、worker、timeout、外部健康和合法慢客户端基线。","Defenders retain incomplete connections, age or progress, workers, timeouts, external health, and legitimate slow-client baselines.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-ST","primary",B("低进度事务跨时间累积内部状态","Low-progress transactions accumulate internal state over time"),P("攻击者用少量周期字节保持状态，网络量被时间稀释而连接/工作槽不释放，形成时空释痕；长窗口连接状态恢复。","The attacker uses sparse periodic bytes to keep state, diluting network volume over time while slots remain allocated, producing spatiotemporal trace dilution; long-window connection state restores it."),["REF-000965","REF-000966","REF-000967"],"high")],"defense":defense(["DET-000231"],["MIT-000206"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000978","CLM-000980","CLM-000982"],"case_refs":[],"reference_refs":["REF-000965","REF-000966","REF-000967","REF-000971","REF-000972"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("证据主要是权威技术与指南而非命名事件；HTTP 以外协议需验证进度语义。","Evidence is mainly authoritative technical documentation rather than a named incident; protocols beyond HTTP require progress-semantics validation."),("合法慢客户端可同形，必须结合状态规模、容量和健康结果。","Legitimate slow clients can be isomorphic and require state scale, capacity, and health outcome."))},"lifecycle":life()})

write(f"{P1499}/subtechniques/NJS-0199-002-input-to-work-cost-amplification/subtechnique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"evasion-subtechnique","id":"NJS-0199-002","parent_ref":"NJT-0199","name":B("输入到工作量成本放大","Input-to-Work Cost Amplification"),"summary":B("攻击者以少量普通外形输入触发不成比例的计算、解析或故障，使端点内部资源失效。","An adversary uses small ordinary-looking inputs to trigger disproportionate computation, parsing, or faults that disable internal endpoint resources."),"aliases":[],"lineage":{"attck_subtechnique_inherited":False},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("输入到工作量成本放大利用算法复杂度、回溯、解析或缺陷，使输入字节/请求数相对内部 CPU、内存、事件循环阻塞或崩溃代价极不对称。稳定变量是输入—工作比，不是漏洞编号或应用层。","Input-to-Work Cost Amplification uses algorithmic complexity, backtracking, parsing, or a flaw to make input bytes or requests grossly asymmetric with internal CPU, memory, event-loop blocking, or crash cost. The stable variable is the input-to-work ratio, not vulnerability ID or application layer.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("输入到工作量成本放大让入口请求长度和数量接近正常，却在内部产生异常工作。流量/速率规则不见明显洪泛；路由、输入结构、每请求时延、资源和健康结果揭示不对称。","Input-to-Work Cost Amplification leaves ingress length and count near normal while generating abnormal internal work. Traffic or rate rules see no flood; route, input structure, per-request duration, resources, and health reveal asymmetry.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入小输入到高工作/故障及实际可用性损失。失败探测、普通慢查询、合法复杂内容和无服务影响的错误不是本项；长期持有未完成状态归兄弟项。","Include small input to high work or fault and actual availability loss. Failed probes, ordinary slow queries, legitimate complex content, and errors without service impact are excluded; long-held incomplete state belongs to the sibling.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("攻击者向易受 ReDoS 的路由或高复杂度 parser 提交精心构造短输入，阻塞共享事件循环或工作线程。","An attacker submits crafted short input to a ReDoS-prone route or complex parser, blocking shared event loops or workers."),P("攻击者需识别高复杂度路径；非回溯算法、输入界限、超时、隔离池和熔断限制效果。","The attacker needs to identify a high-complexity path; nonbacktracking algorithms, input bounds, timeouts, isolation, and circuit breakers constrain it."),P("防守方关联 route/request、输入结构、duration/error、内部资源、崩溃和外部健康；标准 OTel 无每请求 CPU。","Defenders join route and request, input structure, duration or error, internal resources, crash, and external health; standard OTel lacks per-request CPU.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-FD","primary",B("普通小请求外观掩盖异常内部代价","Ordinary small-request appearance disguises abnormal internal cost"),P("攻击输入在长度/数量上接近正常，内部算法/解析却放大工作，入口特征与影响不匹配，形成特征伪装；每请求工作/时延恢复。","Attack input resembles normal length and count while internal algorithms or parsing amplify work, making ingress features mismatch impact and producing feature disguise; per-request work or duration restores it."),["REF-000968","REF-000969","REF-000970"],"high")],"defense":defense(["DET-000231"],["MIT-000206"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000979","CLM-000981","CLM-000982"],"case_refs":[],"reference_refs":["REF-000968","REF-000969","REF-000970","REF-000973","REF-000974","REF-000975"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("ReDoS 高置信成立，跨任意 parser/内核故障泛化为中等；无命名 CASE。","ReDoS is high confidence while generalization across arbitrary parsers or kernel faults is medium; no named CASE is used."),("高时延可由复杂合法输入与代码回归造成，需输入结构和健康结果。","High latency can arise from legitimate complex input or regression and needs input structure and health outcome."))},"lifecycle":life()})

P1529="matrix/tactics/TA0040-impact/techniques/NJT-0200-system-shutdown-reboot"
write(f"{P1529}/technique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"technique","id":"NJT-0200","name":B("系统关机或重启","System Shutdown/Reboot"),"summary":B("攻击者触发主机、VM 或设备生命周期转换造成访问中断，并通过延迟委托或目标外控制面分离决定与结果。","Adversaries trigger host, VM, or device lifecycle transitions causing access interruption and separate decision from outcome through deferred delegation or an out-of-target control plane."),"aliases":["T1529"],"classification":{"tactic_refs":["TA0040"],"origin":{"kind":"attack-adapted","source_attack_id":"T1529","source_attack_version":"19.1"},"decision_ref":"DEC-TA0040-T1529"},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("系统关机或重启是攻击者让主机、虚拟机或网络设备进入关机、重启或等价生命周期转换，使合法用户、服务和会话在转换期间不可访问。直接对象是整个系统实例的生命周期与可用性，不是一个服务状态、崩溃副作用或重启后加载的其他技术。","System Shutdown or Reboot makes a host, virtual machine, or network device enter shutdown, reboot, or an equivalent lifecycle transition so legitimate users, services, and sessions become unavailable during it. The direct object is whole-system lifecycle and availability, not one service state, a crash side effect, or another technique loaded after reboot."),("Niji 关注发起决定与最终转换如何分离：计划任务可让调度器稍后执行，外部 hypervisor/云控制面可在 guest 之外完成。系统接受的正常路径和 reason 也与维护共享，因此状态结果 alone 不含恶意意图。","Niji focuses on separation between the initiating decision and final transition. A scheduled task can execute later through the scheduler, and an external hypervisor or cloud plane can act outside the guest. Accepted lifecycle paths and reason codes are also shared with maintenance, so the state outcome alone contains no malicious intent.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("正常关机/重启会产生 familiar requester、reason、shutdown 和 boot 序列，恶意事件可呈现为补丁或维护。延迟任务把 writer、task、scheduler child 和 boot 分散到不同窗口；外层控制让 guest 只见突然失联，actor 留在 hypervisor。","Normal shutdown or reboot produces familiar requester, reason, shutdown, and boot sequences, allowing a malicious event to resemble patching or maintenance. Deferred tasks distribute writer, task, scheduler child, and boot across windows; outer-plane control leaves the guest seeing disappearance while the actor remains in the hypervisor."),("残余包括本地 caller/privilege/reason、Event 1074/6008/boot ID、任务定义/creator/run instance、WMI correlation、vSphere chainId/user/VM/host、审批和外部健康。跨平面和跨时间关联恢复链。","Residue includes local caller, privilege and reason, Event 1074 or 6008 and boot ID, task definition, creator and run instance, WMI correlation, vSphere chainId, user, VM and host, approval, and external health. Cross-plane and cross-time correlation restores the chain.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入攻击者控制的关机/重启请求被系统或管理面接受并完成，且造成合法访问中断。命令失败、仅写配置、正常补丁/维护/灾备/故障恢复是企图或反例；意外电源、panic 和 watchdog 无恶意生命周期请求时不直接归入。","Include an attacker-controlled shutdown or reboot request accepted and completed by the system or management plane with legitimate-access interruption. Failed commands, configuration-only writes, normal patching, maintenance, DR, or fault recovery are attempts or counterexamples; power loss, panic, and watchdog without a malicious lifecycle request do not directly qualify."),("单服务停止归 NJT-0185；阻止状态转换延长易失立足点归 NJT-0096；Safe Mode 防御缺失归 NJT-0172；资源/漏洞造成的 crash 首先归 NJT-0199。重启只作为后继载荷前提时，本技术仍需独立 availability 结果。","Single-service stop belongs to NJT-0185, inhibited transition preserving a volatile foothold to NJT-0096, Safe Mode defensive omission to NJT-0172, and resource or exploit crash first to NJT-0199. When reboot is only a precursor to another payload, this technique still requires an independent availability outcome.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("恶意软件可注册一次性任务延迟执行 shutdown/reboot，或在 ESXi/云控制面关闭多台 VM 再操作虚拟磁盘。也可本地调用 ExitWindowsEx、shutdown 或 WMI 完成立即转换。","Malware can register a one-time task for delayed shutdown or reboot, or power off many VMs from ESXi or cloud control before operating on virtual disks. It can also call ExitWindowsEx, shutdown, or WMI locally for an immediate transition."),P("攻击者需要本地关机权限、任务 writer，或 hypervisor/cloud power authority，并容忍控制通道与业务中断。最小权限、审批、任务治理、不同权管理面、HA 和快速恢复限制效果。","The attacker needs local shutdown privilege, task-writer authority, or hypervisor or cloud power rights and tolerates control-channel and business interruption. Least privilege, approval, task governance, differently authorized management, HA, and rapid recovery constrain it."),P("防守方保存本地生命周期事件、进程/WMI 调用、任务前后态、boot/uptime、hypervisor events、VM/host inventory、审批和外部健康。只有 guest agent 时，外层 power-off 恰会切断观察。","Defenders retain local lifecycle events, process or WMI calls, task before and after state, boot and uptime, hypervisor events, VM and host inventory, approvals, and external health. A guest-only agent loses observation precisely on outer-plane power-off.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-FD","primary",B("系统接受的生命周期路径呈现常规维护终态","A system-accepted lifecycle path presents an ordinary maintenance terminal state"),P("攻击者使用正常关机/重启路径，OS 或管理面按标准序列停止并记录 reason。状态和理由也由维护生成，难以从终态判断恶意；caller、权限、审批与结果揭示。","The attacker uses a normal shutdown or reboot path, and the OS or management plane stops through a standard sequence and records a reason. Maintenance produces the same state and reason, making terminal-state classification difficult; caller, authority, approval, and outcome reveal it."),["REF-000870","REF-000977","REF-000978"],"medium"),mechanism("NM-ST","secondary",B("调度委托把生命周期决定与结果分散到不同时间和主体","Scheduler delegation disperses lifecycle decision and outcome across time and actors"),P("writer 登记未来任务后退出，调度器稍后以自身/SYSTEM 启动转换。临近结果只见委托主体，短窗口丢失原决定；task ID、definition digest 和 boot 关联恢复。","The writer registers a future task and exits, and the scheduler later starts the transition as itself or SYSTEM. Near the outcome only the delegate is visible and short windows lose the original decision; task ID, definition digest, and boot correlation restore it."),["REF-000601"],"medium")],
"subtechnique_taxonomy":{"narrative":PP(("延迟委托式生命周期转换按 writer 与未来调度执行分离划分，需 task-to-boot 长窗口；目标外控制面生命周期转换按 actor/action 位于 guest 外划分，需 management-plane-to-target 关联。两者可共现但时间与观察域变量不同。","Deferred-Delegated Lifecycle Transition is divided by separation of writer and future scheduled execution and needs long task-to-boot correlation. Out-of-Target Control-Plane Lifecycle Transition is divided by actor and action residing outside the guest and needs management-plane-to-target joins. They can co-occur but time and observation-domain variables differ."),("ATT&CK 无子项。reason camouflage 与维护窗口对齐证据不足而 defer；本地立即转换留父级，平台和命令不形成 NJS。","ATT&CK has no children. Reason camouflage and maintenance-window alignment lack evidence and remain deferred; immediate local transitions remain parent core, and platform or command does not define NJS.")),"coverage":"established","subtechnique_refs":["NJS-0200-001","NJS-0200-002"]},
"defense":defense(["DET-000232"],["MIT-000207"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000983","CLM-000984","CLM-000985","CLM-000986","CLM-000987","CLM-000988"],"case_refs":["CASE-000283","CASE-000284"],"reference_refs":["REF-000870","REF-000601","REF-000294","REF-000977","REF-000978","REF-000979","REF-000980","REF-000981","REF-000982","REF-000983"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("Petya 直接支持计划重启，Play/CISA 支持 ESXi 外层关机；正常维护使用相同路径，必须连接审批和 availability。原因码可被任意填写，不能独立证明伪装。","Petya directly supports scheduled reboot and Play or CISA supports outer ESXi power-off. Normal maintenance uses the same paths, requiring approval and availability joins. Reason codes can be arbitrary and do not independently prove camouflage."),("不同平台生命周期字段不可互换；guest 失联也可由网络/故障造成，需管理面事件确认。","Lifecycle fields are not interchangeable across platforms; guest disappearance can also result from network or faults and needs management-plane confirmation."))},"lifecycle":life()})

write(f"{P1529}/subtechniques/NJS-0200-001-deferred-delegated-lifecycle-transition/subtechnique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"evasion-subtechnique","id":"NJS-0200-001","parent_ref":"NJT-0200","name":B("延迟委托式生命周期转换","Deferred-Delegated Lifecycle Transition"),"summary":B("攻击者登记未来关机或重启任务，让调度器稍后执行，使原始 writer 与生命周期结果分离。","An adversary registers a future shutdown or reboot task so the scheduler executes later, separating the original writer from the lifecycle outcome."),"aliases":[],"lineage":{"attck_subtechnique_inherited":False},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("延迟委托式生命周期转换把恶意关机/重启决定写入计划任务、作业或等价调度对象，由调度器在未来时间以另一个 runtime 主体执行。稳定变量是 writer/definition 与执行/结果跨时间和主体分离，不是 Windows Task Scheduler 产品。","Deferred-Delegated Lifecycle Transition writes a malicious shutdown or reboot decision into a task, job, or equivalent scheduler object for later execution under another runtime principal. The stable variable is separation of writer or definition from execution or outcome across time and actor, not Windows Task Scheduler.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("延迟委托式生命周期转换让临近关机的日志只显示 Task Scheduler/SYSTEM 和 shutdown，原恶意进程可能已退出。短窗口无法回溯任务登记，definition digest、creator、next-run、run instance 和 boot 仍可连接。","Deferred-Delegated Lifecycle Transition leaves logs near shutdown showing Task Scheduler or SYSTEM and shutdown after the malicious writer may have exited. Short windows lose registration, while definition digest, creator, next run, run instance, and boot remain joinable.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入恶意任务/作业定义、后来实际执行的生命周期 action 和 availability 结果。任务被删除/阻断或只启动其他载荷不满足；合法补丁、安装和恢复任务是反例。","Include a malicious task or job definition, later executed lifecycle action, and availability outcome. A deleted or blocked task or one launching another payload does not qualify; legitimate patch, install, and recovery tasks are counterexamples.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("Petya 创建一次性 task，在随机 10–60 分钟后执行强制重启。","Petya creates a one-time task to force reboot 10 to 60 minutes later."),P("攻击者需 task writer 权限和可执行 shutdown 的 runtime；审计、任务签名/allowlist、未来 action 审批和快速撤销限制效果。","The attacker needs task-writer authority and a runtime able to shut down; audit, task signing or allowlists, future-action approval, and rapid revocation constrain it."),P("防守方保留 task old/new、writer、runtime、run instance、scheduled time、Event 1074 和 boot ID，日志需跨任务触发时间。","Defenders retain task old and new state, writer, runtime, run instance, scheduled time, Event 1074, and boot ID across the trigger horizon.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-ST","primary",B("关机决定与结果跨时间和进程身份分散","Shutdown decision and outcome disperse across time and process identity"),P("writer 登记任务后离开，调度器稍后执行；原始痕迹和 availability 结果分散，短窗无法关联。长期 task-to-boot 谱系恢复。","The writer leaves after registering a task and the scheduler executes later; origin trace and availability outcome disperse beyond short windows. Long task-to-boot lineage restores it."),["REF-000601"],"medium")],"defense":defense(["DET-000232"],["MIT-000088","MIT-000207"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000985","CLM-000988"],"case_refs":["CASE-000283"],"reference_refs":["REF-000601","REF-000977","REF-000980"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("Petya 直接支持一次性任务与 10–60 分钟延迟，但其他调度器语义需另证；随机时间本身不证明匿迹动机。","Petya directly supports a one-time task and 10-to-60-minute delay, but other schedulers need separate semantics; random timing alone does not prove stealth motive."),("任务审计缺失、直接后端修改与时钟篡改会削弱关联。","Missing task audit, direct backend manipulation, and clock tampering weaken correlation."))},"lifecycle":life()})

write(f"{P1529}/subtechniques/NJS-0200-002-out-of-target-control-plane-lifecycle-transition/subtechnique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"evasion-subtechnique","id":"NJS-0200-002","parent_ref":"NJT-0200","name":B("目标外控制面生命周期转换","Out-of-Target Control-Plane Lifecycle Transition"),"summary":B("攻击者从 hypervisor 或云控制面关闭/重启目标，使目标内部只见失联而请求者留在外部审计面。","An adversary powers off or reboots a target from a hypervisor or cloud control plane, leaving internal sensors to see disappearance while the requester remains in external audit."),"aliases":[],"lineage":{"attck_subtechnique_inherited":False},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("目标外控制面生命周期转换从目标 OS/guest 外的 hypervisor、云或设备管理面发出 power action，使目标实例完成关机/重启。稳定变量是 actor/action 与受影响系统观察域分离，不是 ESXi 或云厂商。","Out-of-Target Control-Plane Lifecycle Transition issues a power action from a hypervisor, cloud, or device plane outside the target OS or guest and completes target shutdown or reboot. The stable variable is separation of actor and action from the affected system observation domain, not ESXi or cloud provider.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("目标外控制面生命周期转换使 guest/端点 agent 在电源事件前没有本地 requester，随后随系统离线；内部只见 heartbeat/网络消失。hypervisor event、user、chainId、VM/host 和 auditId 保留外部因果。","Out-of-Target Control-Plane Lifecycle Transition leaves the guest or endpoint agent without a local requester before it disappears with the system; internally only heartbeat or network loss remains. Hypervisor event, user, chainId, VM or host, and auditId preserve external causality.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入外部管理面成功 power-off/reboot、明确目标和 availability 结果。Guest 内 WMI/命令、管理面登录无 action、网络断开或 host 故障不满足。","Include a successful external management-plane power-off or reboot with an explicit target and availability outcome. Guest-local WMI or command, management login without action, network loss, or host fault do not qualify.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("勒索操作者控制 ESXi 后枚举并关闭运行 VM，再操作 VMDK；VM 内监控随关机中断。","A ransomware operator controls ESXi, enumerates and powers off running VMs, and then operates on VMDKs; in-guest monitoring stops with power."),P("攻击者需 hypervisor/cloud power 权限和目标映射；MFA、JIT、分离角色、不可变审计和 HA 限制效果。","The attacker needs hypervisor or cloud power authority and target mapping; MFA, JIT, separated roles, immutable audit, and HA constrain it."),P("防守方连接管理面 session/event、actor、host/VM、power state、guest heartbeat 和业务健康；只有 guest telemetry 形成盲区。","Defenders join management session or event, actor, host and VM, power state, guest heartbeat, and business health; guest-only telemetry creates the blind spot.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-BT","primary",B("外部控制面跨越目标系统生命周期观察边界","An external control plane crosses the target system's lifecycle observation boundary"),P("攻击者从外层管理面执行 power action，目标本地不生成原始请求并很快失去传感器。关键因果留在不同权控制面，形成行为透明；跨管理事件和 guest 结果关联恢复。","The attacker executes the power action from an outer management plane, leaving no local original request and quickly removing target sensors. Critical causality remains in a differently authorized plane, producing behavioral transparency; joining management events to guest outcome restores it."),["REF-000981","REF-000982","REF-000983"],"high")],"defense":defense(["DET-000232"],["MIT-000207"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000986","CLM-000988"],"case_refs":["CASE-000284"],"reference_refs":["REF-000981","REF-000982","REF-000983"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("Play 通告和 VMware 资料支持 ESXi 场景，但其他控制面的事件字段与权限需独立验证。","Play reporting and VMware sources support ESXi, while other control planes need independent field and authority validation."),("guest 失联也可由网络、host 故障或迁移造成，必须有成功 power event。","Guest disappearance can also arise from network, host fault, or migration and requires a successful power event."))},"lifecycle":life()})

P1531="matrix/tactics/TA0040-impact/techniques/NJT-0201-account-access-removal"
write(f"{P1531}/technique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"technique","id":"NJT-0201","name":B("移除账户访问","Account Access Removal"),"summary":B("攻击者保留既有账户外观却置换合法 owner 的认证器或撤除授权边，使合法主体实际失去访问。","Adversaries preserve the appearance of an existing account while displacing the legitimate owner's authenticators or evicting authorization edges so the principal actually loses access."),"aliases":["T1531"],"classification":{"tactic_refs":["TA0040"],"origin":{"kind":"attack-adapted","source_attack_id":"T1531","source_attack_version":"19.1"},"decision_ref":"DEC-TA0040-T1531"},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("移除账户访问是攻击者删除、替换或撤销既有合法用户、管理员、服务主体或租户 owner 所需的认证器、恢复路径、角色、组、委托或访问策略，使其在变更后实际无法认证或访问预期资源。直接对象是合法主体的访问可用性，不是攻击者能否继续使用该账户。","Account Access Removal deletes, replaces, or revokes authenticators, recovery paths, roles, groups, delegations, or access policy needed by an existing legitimate user, administrator, service principal, or tenant owner so the principal actually cannot authenticate or access expected resources afterward. The direct object is availability of legitimate-principal access, not whether the attacker can continue using the account."),("Niji 关注账户身份/启用状态与 owner 真实访问之间的错位：认证器被排他置换时账户仍存在，授权边撤除时认证仍可成功。正式完成门槛是合法主体 post-state 失败；管理变更 alone 只是风险。","Niji focuses on mismatch between account identity or enabled state and actual owner access. The account remains present after exclusive authenticator displacement, and authentication may still succeed after authorization-edge eviction. Formal completion requires legitimate-principal post-state failure; an administrative mutation alone is risk.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("认证器置换保留账户名称、年龄、启用状态和攻击者控制方法，粗粒度目录监控显示熟悉身份；owner 密码/MFA/恢复方法已失效。授权边撤除保留认证成功和账户健康，资源求值阶段才 deny。单看账户状态或登录成功都会遗漏一类影响。","Authenticator displacement preserves account name, age, enabled state, and attacker-controlled methods, so coarse directory monitoring sees a familiar identity while owner password, MFA, or recovery path no longer works. Authorization-edge eviction preserves successful authentication and account health until resource evaluation denies access. Account-state-only or successful-sign-in-only views each miss one impact."),("残余包括 directoryAudit initiator/targets/modifiedProperties/correlationId、认证方法/角色/组 old-new、signIn status/device/risk/CA、资源 deny、owner/break-glass 测试与审批。不可变审计和周期图快照恢复差分。","Residue includes directoryAudit initiator, targets, modifiedProperties and correlationId, authentication-method or role or group old and new state, signIn status, device, risk and CA, resource denial, owner or break-glass tests, and approval. Immutable audit and periodic graph snapshots restore the differential.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入攻击者控制的持久身份状态负向变化以及合法 owner 实际认证/授权失败。只重置密码但 owner 仍有其他路径、删除会话 token 后可重新登录、暂时风险阻断或失败变更不完成。合法 offboarding、fraud response、账户恢复、角色到期与法务 hold 是反例。","Include adversary-controlled negative durable identity-state mutation and actual legitimate-owner authentication or authorization failure. Password reset with another owner path, session-token revocation followed by reauthentication, temporary risk block, or failed mutation does not complete. Legitimate offboarding, fraud response, account recovery, entitlement expiry, and legal hold are counterexamples."),("新增并行认证器/授权边以维持攻击者访问归 NJT-0083；全局认证决策篡改归 NJT-0093；中央防御策略损伤归 NJT-0125；权限提升需证明攻击者新增 authority。一个事件可并记，但合法 owner lockout 证据不可省。","Adding parallel authenticators or authorization edges for attacker persistence belongs to NJT-0083, global authentication-decision changes to NJT-0093, central defensive-policy impairment to NJT-0125, and privilege escalation requires added attacker authority. One incident can co-map, but legitimate-owner lockout evidence remains required.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("攻击者可使用 SSPR 重置密码、删除 owner 原认证方法并注册攻击者方法，或在建立自己管理员后移除其他 Global Administrators/关键组和委托，使组织失去租户控制。","An attacker can use SSPR to reset a password, remove original owner methods, and enroll attacker methods, or after creating its own admin remove other Global Administrators, critical groups, and delegations so the organization loses tenant control."),P("攻击者需要身份恢复/认证方法或角色/组/委托写权限，并了解 owner 的全部替代路径与传播延迟。审批、PIM/JIT、方法数量/恢复策略、独立 break-glass 和不可变日志限制效果。","The attacker needs identity-recovery or authenticator or role, group, or delegation write authority and knowledge of all owner alternatives and propagation delay. Approval, PIM or JIT, method count and recovery policy, independent break-glass, and immutable logs constrain it."),P("防守方连接状态变更、old-new 图、审批、owner sign-in、资源访问 deny 与 break-glass 演练。平台若不暴露 method ID，只能主体级推断；短留存会遗漏延迟 lockout。","Defenders join state mutation, old-new graph, approval, owner sign-in, resource denial, and break-glass exercises. Platforms without method IDs permit principal-level inference only; short retention misses delayed lockout.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-FD","primary",B("熟悉账户实体掩盖合法 owner 认证路径被置换","A familiar account entity disguises displacement of the legitimate owner's authentication path"),P("攻击者保留账户身份和启用外观，只替换 owner 认证/恢复方法。粗粒度实体规则看似正常，恶意与合法控制共享主体特征，形成特征伪装；方法 old-new 和 owner 失败揭示。","The attacker preserves account identity and enabled appearance while replacing owner authentication or recovery methods. Coarse entity rules remain normal and malicious and legitimate control share principal features, producing feature disguise; method old-new and owner failure reveal it."),["REF-000167","REF-000985","REF-000986"],"high"),mechanism("NM-BT","secondary",B("认证成功与资源授权拒绝分布在不同决策平面","Successful authentication and resource denial are distributed across decision planes"),P("攻击者撤除授权边，身份提供者仍认证熟悉主体，资源面才拒绝访问。只看 sign-in health 的守方看不到 Impact，需连接图变化和 resource deny，形成行为透明。","The attacker evicts authorization edges, leaving the identity provider authenticating a familiar principal while the resource plane denies access. Sign-in-health-only defenders miss Impact and need graph mutation plus resource denial, producing behavioral transparency."),["REF-000103","REF-000985","REF-000986"],"high")],
"subtechnique_taxonomy":{"narrative":PP(("身份保留式认证器置换锁定改变 owner 能否用密码/MFA/恢复方法认证，账户仍存在；授权图边撤除锁定改变已认证主体能否通过角色/组/委托/策略访问资源。两个终态和恢复动作不同。","Identity-Preserving Authenticator-Displacement Lockout changes whether the owner can authenticate with password, MFA, or recovery methods while the account remains. Authorization-Graph Edge-Eviction Lockout changes whether an authenticated principal can access resources through roles, groups, delegations, or policy. Their terminal states and recovery actions differ."),("ATT&CK 无子项。账户类型、平台、密码与 MFA 介质不形成 NJS；session-only revocation 不持久，新增攻击者访问状态由 NJT-0083 负责。","ATT&CK has no children. Account type, platform, password versus MFA medium do not define NJS; session-only revocation is not durable and NJT-0083 owns added attacker access state.")),"coverage":"established","subtechnique_refs":["NJS-0201-001","NJS-0201-002"]},
"defense":defense(["DET-000233"],["MIT-000063"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000989","CLM-000990","CLM-000991","CLM-000992","CLM-000993","CLM-000994"],"case_refs":["CASE-000285","CASE-000286"],"reference_refs":["REF-000984","REF-000103","REF-000167","REF-000985","REF-000986","REF-000987","REF-000790","REF-000376","REF-000143"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("Microsoft 案例高置信支持两类锁定结果，但租户字段和方法 ID 并非所有平台一致。管理员变更不等于 owner 已失败，必须验证 post-state。","Microsoft cases strongly support both lockout outcomes, but tenant fields and method IDs are not uniform across platforms. An administrative mutation does not equal owner failure and post-state must be verified."),("正常 offboarding、账户恢复和 fraud response 产生相似负向变化；审批、owner、时限和 break-glass 结果决定反例。","Normal offboarding, account recovery, and fraud response create similar negative mutations; approval, owner, duration, and break-glass outcome determine counterexamples."))},"lifecycle":life()})

write(f"{P1531}/subtechniques/NJS-0201-001-identity-preserving-authenticator-displacement-lockout/subtechnique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"evasion-subtechnique","id":"NJS-0201-001","parent_ref":"NJT-0201","name":B("身份保留式认证器置换锁定","Identity-Preserving Authenticator-Displacement Lockout"),"summary":B("攻击者保留账户实体和启用状态，却排他替换 owner 认证与恢复方法，使合法主体无法登录。","An adversary preserves the account entity and enabled state while exclusively replacing owner authentication and recovery methods so the legitimate principal cannot sign in."),"aliases":[],"lineage":{"attck_subtechnique_inherited":False},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("身份保留式认证器置换锁定删除/替换 owner 密码、MFA、恢复邮箱/电话或其他方法，同时账户仍存在启用且可能由攻击者方法控制。稳定变量是身份实体与合法认证路径分离，不是认证器类型。","Identity-Preserving Authenticator-Displacement Lockout deletes or replaces owner password, MFA, recovery email or phone, or another method while the account remains present and enabled and may be controlled by attacker methods. The stable variable is separation of identity entity from the legitimate authentication path, not authenticator type.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("身份保留式认证器置换锁定让目录清单仍显示熟悉账户，攻击者登录甚至显示成功，合法 owner 的失败只在登录/恢复平面出现。方法 old-new、发起者、审批和 owner failure 恢复差分。","Identity-Preserving Authenticator-Displacement Lockout leaves the directory showing a familiar account and may show attacker sign-ins succeeding while legitimate-owner failure appears only in sign-in or recovery planes. Method old-new, initiator, approval, and owner failure restore the differential.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入 owner 全部有效认证/恢复路径被未经授权置换并实际登录失败。增加并行方法但 owner 仍能登录归 NJT-0083；单 session 撤销或临时风险 challenge 不满足。","Include unauthorized displacement of all effective owner authentication or recovery paths with actual sign-in failure. Adding a parallel method while the owner still signs in belongs to NJT-0083; one-session revocation or temporary risk challenge does not qualify.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("攻击者滥用 SSPR 重置密码、删除原 MFA 并注册自己的方法，保留同一账户名。","An attacker abuses SSPR to reset a password, remove original MFA, and enroll its own methods under the same account name."),P("攻击者需恢复/方法管理权限并识别所有路径；独立 break-glass、强审批和方法变更通知限制效果。","The attacker needs recovery or method-management authority and knowledge of all paths; independent break-glass, strong approval, and method-change notification constrain it."),P("防守方连接 directoryAudit modifiedProperties、发起者、correlation、owner signIn failure、method inventory 和审批。","Defenders join directoryAudit modifiedProperties, initiator, correlation, owner sign-in failure, method inventory, and approval.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-FD","primary",B("保留账户身份外观掩盖 owner 认证器被排他替换","Preserved account appearance disguises exclusive replacement of owner authenticators"),P("账户名/启用状态不变，目录和实体信誉保持熟悉，但 owner 路径已失效，形成特征伪装；方法版本与登录失败揭示。","Account name and enabled state remain, preserving directory and entity reputation while owner paths fail, producing feature disguise; method versions and sign-in failure reveal it."),["REF-000167","REF-000985","REF-000986"],"high")],"defense":defense(["DET-000233"],["MIT-000063"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000990","CLM-000992","CLM-000994"],"case_refs":["CASE-000286"],"reference_refs":["REF-000167","REF-000985","REF-000986","REF-000987"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("Storm-2949 支持 SSPR/MFA 置换和 owner 失败；其他平台需映射等价 method 与恢复字段。","Storm-2949 supports SSPR or MFA displacement and owner failure; other platforms need equivalent method and recovery fields."),("signIn 日志可能无精确 method ID，需主体级和状态快照关联。","Sign-in logs may lack exact method IDs and require principal-level and snapshot correlation."))},"lifecycle":life()})

write(f"{P1531}/subtechniques/NJS-0201-002-authorization-graph-edge-eviction-lockout/subtechnique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"evasion-subtechnique","id":"NJS-0201-002","parent_ref":"NJT-0201","name":B("授权图边撤除锁定","Authorization-Graph Edge-Eviction Lockout"),"summary":B("攻击者移除角色、组、委托或策略边，使合法主体仍能认证但在资源求值时失去访问。","An adversary removes role, group, delegation, or policy edges so a legitimate principal can still authenticate but loses access at resource evaluation."),"aliases":[],"lineage":{"attck_subtechnique_inherited":False},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("授权图边撤除锁定删除既有主体依赖的角色、组成员、委托、owner 或 policy edge，导致认证后无法管理/访问资源。稳定变量是认证成功与授权失败跨决策平面分离，不是角色名称。","Authorization-Graph Edge-Eviction Lockout deletes roles, group memberships, delegations, ownership, or policy edges needed by an existing principal, causing post-authentication resource denial. The stable variable is separation of successful authentication from authorization failure across decision planes, not role name.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("授权图边撤除锁定保留账户与 sign-in 正常外观，Impact 在资源 deny 时才显现。只监控认证健康的守方会延迟理解；图 old-new、资源求值和 break-glass 结果恢复。","Authorization-Graph Edge-Eviction Lockout preserves normal account and sign-in appearance and reveals Impact only at resource denial. Authentication-health-only defenders delay understanding; graph old-new, resource evaluation, and break-glass results restore it.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入未经授权撤除关键访问边与实际资源 deny。正常岗位变更、PIM 到期、offboarding 和 least-privilege 清理是反例；认证器失效归兄弟项。","Include unauthorized removal of critical access edges and actual resource denial. Normal role change, PIM expiry, offboarding, and least-privilege cleanup are counterexamples; authenticator failure belongs to the sibling.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("攻击者建立自身管理员后，移除其他 Global Admin 或关键 owner/group/delegation，使组织仍能登录但无法管理租户/资源。","After establishing its own administrator, an attacker removes other Global Admins or critical owners, groups, or delegations so the organization can sign in but cannot administer tenants or resources."),P("攻击者需 role/group/policy 写权和依赖图知识；PIM、双人审批、最小写权和多个独立 emergency accounts 限制效果。","The attacker needs role, group, or policy write authority and graph knowledge; PIM, dual approval, least write authority, and multiple independent emergency accounts constrain it."),P("防守方保存 graph 快照、directoryAudit、resource deny、owner 清单和 break-glass 测试，并关联 propagation。","Defenders retain graph snapshots, directoryAudit, resource denial, owner inventory, and break-glass tests and account for propagation.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-BT","primary",B("授权边变化在资源决策平面隐藏于正常认证之后","Authorization-edge mutation hides in a resource decision plane after normal authentication"),P("身份提供者继续认证熟悉主体，资源平面因边撤除拒绝访问。防守若止于 sign-in success 看不到 Impact，形成行为透明；图变化到 deny 的关联恢复。","The identity provider continues authenticating a familiar principal while the resource plane denies access after edge eviction. Defenders stopping at sign-in success miss Impact, producing behavioral transparency; graph-change-to-deny correlation restores it."),["REF-000103","REF-000985","REF-000986"],"high")],"defense":defense(["DET-000233"],["MIT-000063"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000991","CLM-000993","CLM-000994"],"case_refs":["CASE-000285"],"reference_refs":["REF-000103","REF-000985","REF-000986","REF-000987"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("DEV-0537 支持 Global Admin 撤除与 tenant lockout；其他资源图需验证 deny 与传播。","DEV-0537 supports Global Admin eviction and tenant lockout; other resource graphs require denial and propagation validation."),("资源 deny 可由策略、许可或故障造成，必须连接具体 edge 和审批。","Resource denial can arise from policy, licensing, or faults and must join a specific edge and approval."))},"lifecycle":life()})

P1561="matrix/tactics/TA0040-impact/techniques/NJT-0202-disk-wipe"
write(f"{P1561}/technique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"technique","id":"NJT-0202","name":B("磁盘擦除","Disk Wipe"),"summary":B("攻击者在块或磁盘层破坏内容和关键结构，并通过少量关键写入或可恢复性伪装降低早期识别与正确响应。","Adversaries destroy block-level content and critical disk structures while minimal critical writes or recoverability pretext reduce early recognition and correct response."),"aliases":["T1561"],"classification":{"tactic_refs":["TA0040"],"origin":{"kind":"attack-adapted","source_attack_id":"T1561","source_attack_version":"19.1"},"decision_ref":"DEC-TA0040-T1561"},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("磁盘擦除是攻击者直接写入、丢弃、重新初始化或不可恢复地变换物理盘、块设备或卷，使内容、引导、分区或文件系统元数据不能支持原有系统/数据用途。直接对象是介质级结构与可用性，不是单个路径对象；设备仍枚举或通电不否定磁盘状态已失效。","Disk Wipe writes, discards, reinitializes, or irreversibly transforms a physical disk, block device, or volume so content, boot, partition, or filesystem metadata no longer supports the original system or data purpose. The direct object is media-level structure and availability, not one path object; continued enumeration or power does not negate invalid disk state."),("Niji 关注很少关键块写入造成远大于写量的损失，以及不可恢复擦除被呈现为可支付/可解密的勒索。写零、随机数、加密、格式化、IOCTL、驱动和重启是实现；块状态与合法可用性结果共同区分完成、企图和维护。","Niji focuses on small critical-block writes causing loss far beyond write volume and irreversible wiping presented as payable or decryptable ransomware. Zeroes, random data, encryption, formatting, IOCTL, driver, and reboot are implementations; block state plus legitimate availability outcome separates completion, attempt, and maintenance.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("关键引导、分区和文件系统元数据占介质很小，却决定整个卷能否定位解释。集中写入这些区间时，文件级修改和全盘写量阈值没有与结果相称信号；原始句柄、驱动/IOCTL、扇区和 metadata 校验保留因果。","Critical boot, partition, and filesystem metadata occupies little media but determines whether the entire volume can be located and interpreted. Concentrated writes produce no file-level or full-disk-volume signal proportional to impact; raw handles, driver or IOCTL, sectors, and metadata validation preserve causality."),("勒索画面、安装 ID、扩展名或解密承诺可把不可恢复擦除呈现为密钥控制事件，守方可能追踪支付/解密而延迟保全介质和裸机重建。块状态、key/ID 来源与恢复代码揭示矛盾。","A ransom screen, installation ID, extension, or decryption promise can present irreversible wiping as key custody, causing defenders to pursue payment or decryption and delay media preservation and bare-metal rebuild. Block state, key or ID provenance, and recovery code expose the contradiction.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入对物理盘、块设备或卷的未授权写入/丢弃/初始化，以及分区表、引导记录、文件系统、块内容、挂载/启动或业务数据集失效。仅驱动加载、磁盘枚举、raw open/read 或失败 IOCTL 是前置/企图；合法格式化/退役需匹配 owner、工单、范围和预期新状态。","Include unauthorized write, discard, or initialization of a physical disk, block device, or volume and failure of partition table, boot record, filesystem, block content, mount or boot, or business dataset. Driver load, disk enumeration, raw open or read, or failed IOCTL is precursor or attempt; legitimate format or decommission needs matching owner, ticket, scope, and expected new state."),("路径级文件/对象损失归 NJT-0156，固件归 NJT-0188，恢复角色对象归 NJT-0186，只读 raw view 归 NJT-0108。可由掌握密钥恢复的密文归 NJT-0157；无 key 且直接破坏盘状态可归本技术，但需验证介质与不可恢复性。","Path-level file or object loss belongs to NJT-0156, firmware to NJT-0188, recovery-role objects to NJT-0186, and read-only raw views to NJT-0108. Ciphertext recoverable with a held key belongs to NJT-0157; encryption with no key and direct disk-state destruction can belong here with verified media and irrecoverability.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("攻击者取得管理员/内核/raw-write 权限后，覆写 MBR、GPT、MFT、位图/日志或全盘，使主机不可启动或卷不可挂载。HermeticWiper 借 EaseUS 驱动和 DeviceIoControl；GigaWiper 重建分区并覆写物理盘；ExPetr 用随机安装 ID 呈现虚假可恢复性。","After obtaining administrator, kernel, or raw-write authority, an attacker overwrites MBR, GPT, MFT, bitmap or log, or the full disk, making the host unbootable or volume unmountable. HermeticWiper used EaseUS drivers and DeviceIoControl; GigaWiper reinitialized partitions and overwrote disks; ExPetr used a random installation ID to present false recoverability."),P("攻击者需要 raw write、storage IOCTL、driver-load/root 或存储控制权与目标/metadata 知识；伪装还需可信勒索叙事。只读/受保护设备、应用控制、内核遥测、冗余 metadata 与独立映像限制效果。","The attacker needs raw write, storage IOCTL, driver-load or root, or storage control and target and metadata knowledge; camouflage also needs a credible ransom story. Read-only or protected devices, application control, kernel telemetry, redundant metadata, and independent images constrain it."),P("防守方观察进程/账户、raw open、驱动签名、IOCTL、块 I/O device/sector/length/direction、分区/文件系统清单、metadata hash/CRC、mount/boot/health、勒索工件和重启。完整块追踪昂贵且主机可随盘失效，因此关键区间和外部汇聚优先。","Defenders observe process or account, raw open, driver signature, IOCTL, block-I/O device, sector, length and direction, partition or filesystem inventory, metadata hash or CRC, mount, boot or health, ransom artifacts, and reboot. Full block tracing is expensive and host telemetry can die with the disk, so critical extents and external collection take priority.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-BT","primary",B("关键块破坏发生在文件级观察之外","Critical-block destruction occurs outside file-level observation"),P("攻击者少量 raw 写入 MBR/GPT/MFT 等区间，痕迹从大量文件变化变为设备句柄、驱动/IOCTL 和有限扇区；文件传感器看不到决定卷可用性的因果，形成行为透明。","The attacker performs a few raw writes to MBR, GPT, or MFT, changing traces from many file changes to a device handle, driver or IOCTL, and limited sectors. File sensors cannot see the cause deciding volume availability, producing behavioral transparency."),["REF-000988","REF-000989","REF-000990"],"high"),mechanism("NM-FD","secondary",B("可恢复勒索外观掩盖不可恢复磁盘毁坏","A recoverable-ransomware appearance disguises irreversible disk destruction"),P("攻击者显示勒索、ID 或解密状态，事件看似可用 key 恢复，但实现不保留恢复材料或并行擦除结构。呈现与真实状态冲突形成特征伪装；块状态与 key/恢复语义揭示。","The attacker displays ransom, an ID, or decryption state so the event appears key-recoverable while the implementation retains no recovery material or wipes structures. The conflict between presentation and reality produces feature disguise; block state and key or recovery semantics expose it."),["REF-000989","REF-000990","REF-000991"],"high")],
"subtechnique_taxonomy":{"narrative":PP(("关键元数据最小写入式毁坏按破坏覆盖与全盘影响不对称划分，需 raw I/O 与结构完整性；可恢复性话术伪装式擦除按呈现与实际恢复语义冲突划分，需 key/ID 和块状态验证。","Critical-Metadata Minimal-Write Destruction is divided by asymmetry between write coverage and disk impact and needs raw I/O and structure integrity. Recoverability-Pretext Wipe Camouflage is divided by conflict between presentation and actual recovery semantics and needs key or ID and block-state validation."),("T1561.001/.002 内容/结构不导入。全盘覆写和普通结构初始化留父级，signed driver 是路径，写入模式和 device sanitize 证据不足，恢复对象/固件由相邻 owner 负责。","T1561.001 and .002 content or structure are not imported. Full-disk overwrite and ordinary structure initialization remain parent core, signed drivers are a path, overwrite patterns and device sanitize lack evidence, and recovery objects or firmware have adjacent owners.")),"coverage":"established","subtechnique_refs":["NJS-0202-001","NJS-0202-002"]},
"defense":defense(["DET-000105","DET-000234"],["MIT-000107","MIT-000158","MIT-000208"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000995","CLM-000996","CLM-000997","CLM-000998","CLM-000999","CLM-001000"],"case_refs":["CASE-000287","CASE-000288","CASE-000289"],"reference_refs":["REF-000898","REF-000988","REF-000989","REF-000990","REF-000991","REF-000992","REF-000993","REF-000994","REF-000840","REF-000366","REF-000475","REF-000995","REF-000996"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("HermeticWiper 同时更广泛擦除，因此只可断言 512-byte MBR 破坏足以启动失败，不把全部损失归于最少写入。ExPetr 高置信证明话术/ID 与可恢复性冲突；不同 wiper 呈现不能模板化。","HermeticWiper also wipes broadly, so only sufficiency of a 512-byte MBR change for boot failure can be claimed, not all loss attributed to minimal writes. ExPetr strongly establishes presentation or ID conflict with recoverability; different wiper presentations cannot be templated."),("Linux 字段是可实施示例；Windows 默认 EDR 无逐扇区字段，必须用自建/内核传感器。合法格式化与退役是强反例。","Linux fields are implementable examples. Windows default EDR lacks per-sector fields and needs custom or kernel sensing. Legitimate formatting and decommission are strong counterexamples."))},"lifecycle":life()})

write(f"{P1561}/subtechniques/NJS-0202-001-critical-metadata-minimal-write-destruction/subtechnique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"evasion-subtechnique","id":"NJS-0202-001","parent_ref":"NJT-0202","name":B("关键元数据最小写入式毁坏","Critical-Metadata Minimal-Write Destruction"),"summary":B("攻击者只破坏少量引导、分区或文件系统关键块，即造成整个盘或卷不可用。","An adversary destroys only small boot, partition, or filesystem critical extents yet makes the entire disk or volume unavailable."),"aliases":[],"lineage":{"attck_subtechnique_inherited":False},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("关键元数据最小写入式毁坏把 raw 写入集中在占介质很小但决定启动、分区解析、文件系统定位或一致性的区间，使少量字节变化造成全盘/卷失效。稳定变量是写入覆盖率与可用性损失不对称，不是 MBR/GPT/MFT 名称。","Critical-Metadata Minimal-Write Destruction concentrates raw writes on small extents controlling boot, partition parsing, filesystem location, or consistency so few changed bytes disable the disk or volume. The stable variable is asymmetry between write coverage and availability loss, not MBR, GPT, or MFT names.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("关键元数据最小写入式毁坏不会产生与全盘损失相称的写入量或文件事件。少量扇区、驱动/IOCTL 和 metadata 校验变化决定结果；只看文件/总写量的守方低估风险。","Critical-Metadata Minimal-Write Destruction produces neither write volume nor file events proportional to whole-disk loss. A few sectors, driver or IOCTL, and metadata-validation changes decide outcome; file or total-volume-only defenders underestimate risk.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入少量关键块的未经授权破坏、结构校验失败及 mount/boot/volume 结果。全盘内容覆写留父级；正常修复、分区转换和格式化是反例。","Include unauthorized destruction of a small critical extent, failed structure validation, and mount, boot, or volume outcome. Full-disk content overwrite remains parent core; normal repair, partition conversion, and formatting are counterexamples.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("HermeticWiper 借驱动写入 MBR/MFT 等，首 512 字节 MBR 破坏足以使系统不可启动。","HermeticWiper used a driver to write MBR and MFT areas; corruption of the first 512-byte MBR was sufficient to make a system unbootable."),P("攻击者需 raw write/driver 和关键布局知识；backup headers、冗余 metadata、写保护与结构验证限制效果。","The attacker needs raw-write or driver authority and layout knowledge; backup headers, redundant metadata, write protection, and structure validation constrain it."),P("防守方关联 raw open、driver/IOCTL、sector/length、metadata hash/CRC 和 mount/boot。文件日志不能替代块 telemetry。","Defenders join raw open, driver or IOCTL, sector and length, metadata hash or CRC, and mount or boot. File logs cannot replace block telemetry.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-BT","primary",B("少量关键块写入跨越文件级观察并造成全卷损失","A few critical-block writes cross file-level observation and cause whole-volume loss"),P("攻击者不遍历文件而直接改变结构块，文件传感器看不到路径级因果，影响远大于写量，形成行为透明；offset 和结构校验恢复。","The attacker changes structural blocks without traversing files, leaving file sensors without path-level causality and impact far greater than write volume, producing behavioral transparency; offsets and structure validation restore it."),["REF-000988","REF-000989","REF-000992"],"high")],"defense":defense(["DET-000105"],["MIT-000107","MIT-000158"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000996","CLM-000998","CLM-001000"],"case_refs":["CASE-000287"],"reference_refs":["REF-000988","REF-000989","REF-000992","REF-000993","REF-000994","REF-000840","REF-000366","REF-000995","REF-000996"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("HermeticWiper 证明关键结构与启动失败，但同时更广泛写入，不能把所有损失只归于首 512 字节。","HermeticWiper establishes critical structures and boot failure but also writes more broadly, so not all loss can be attributed only to the first 512 bytes."),("跨文件系统推广为中等，需各结构的完整性/冗余语义。","Cross-filesystem generalization is medium and needs each structure's integrity and redundancy semantics."))},"lifecycle":life()})

write(f"{P1561}/subtechniques/NJS-0202-002-recoverability-pretext-wipe-camouflage/subtechnique.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"evasion-subtechnique","id":"NJS-0202-002","parent_ref":"NJT-0202","name":B("可恢复性话术伪装式擦除","Recoverability-Pretext Wipe Camouflage"),"summary":B("攻击者用勒索、安装 ID 或解密承诺把不可恢复擦除呈现为可支付、可解密的加密事件。","An adversary uses ransom, installation IDs, or decryption promises to present an irreversible wipe as a payable, decryptable encryption event."),"aliases":[],"lineage":{"attck_subtechnique_inherited":False},
"definition_and_concept":PP(("可恢复性话术伪装式擦除在实际磁盘破坏不保留可用 key/恢复路径时，仍展示勒索、ID、扩展名或解密承诺，使事件被理解为密钥控制而非不可逆介质毁坏。稳定变量是呈现的可恢复性与真实恢复语义冲突。","Recoverability-Pretext Wipe Camouflage displays ransom, IDs, extensions, or decryption promises even though disk destruction retains no usable key or recovery path, causing the event to be understood as key custody rather than irreversible media destruction. The stable variable is conflict between presented recoverability and actual recovery semantics.")),
"stealth_characteristics":PP(("可恢复性话术伪装式擦除让初始工件与普通 ransomware 相似，守方可能优先追踪支付/解密并延迟介质保全与裸机重建。随机 ID、未保存 key/IV、块结构毁坏和不可达恢复代码揭示矛盾。","Recoverability-Pretext Wipe Camouflage makes initial artifacts resemble ordinary ransomware, causing defenders to prioritize payment or decryption and delay media preservation and bare-metal rebuild. Random IDs, unretained keys or IVs, destroyed structures, and unreachable recovery code expose the contradiction.")),
"scope_boundary_definition":PP(("纳入实际不可恢复块破坏、明确可恢复性呈现和两者冲突。只有勒索字条/扩展名，或攻击者持有真实可用 key 的磁盘加密不满足；后者归 NJT-0157。","Include actual irreversible block destruction, explicit recoverability presentation, and their conflict. A ransom note or extension alone, or disk encryption with a real usable attacker-held key, does not qualify; the latter belongs to NJT-0157.")),
"application_scenarios_and_threat_model":context(P("ExPetr 显示安装 ID 与勒索，但 ID 随机且无法生成解密；GigaWiper/PartyTicket 等也可用勒索外观掩护擦除。","ExPetr displayed an installation ID and ransom while the ID was random and could not enable decryption; GigaWiper or PartyTicket can also use ransomware appearance around wiping."),P("攻击者需完成擦除并部署可信的恢复叙事；真实 key provenance、样本逆向和快速块状态验证限制误导。","The attacker needs to complete wiping and deploy a credible recovery narrative; real key provenance, reverse engineering, and rapid block-state validation constrain deception."),P("防守方连接 ransom artifacts、ID/key/IV 生成与保存、恢复代码、块 metadata 和恢复试验；不执行会扩大损失的未验证解密器。","Defenders join ransom artifacts, ID or key or IV generation and retention, recovery code, block metadata, and safe recovery testing and avoid unverified decryptors that can worsen loss.")),
"stealth_mechanisms":[mechanism("NM-FD","primary",B("可解密勒索外观掩盖不可恢复介质毁坏","A decryptable-ransomware appearance disguises irreversible media destruction"),P("攻击者提供 familiar ransomware 特征但不保留恢复材料，守方从表象推断错误响应，形成特征伪装；key/ID 来源和块状态揭示。","The attacker supplies familiar ransomware features without recovery material, leading defenders to infer the wrong response and producing feature disguise; key or ID provenance and block state reveal it."),["REF-000989","REF-000990","REF-000991"],"high")],"defense":defense(["DET-000234"],["MIT-000208"]),"evidence":{"claim_refs":["CLM-000997","CLM-000999","CLM-001000"],"case_refs":["CASE-000288","CASE-000289"],"reference_refs":["REF-000989","REF-000990","REF-000991","REF-000475"]},"research":{"limitations":PP(("ExPetr 高置信证明随机 ID 与不可恢复性；不同 wiper 的 key/IV 和呈现方式不可互换。","ExPetr strongly establishes random IDs and irrecoverability; key or IV and presentation are not interchangeable across wipers."),("缺样本/块证据时，不能从勒索字条 alone 判定 wipe。","Without sample or block evidence, a ransom note alone cannot establish wiping."))},"lifecycle":life()})

def req(t,n,c,f): return {"source_type":t,"name":n,"channel":c,"required_fields":f}
def strategy(n,slug,name,summary,description,targets,analytics,refs): write(f"detections/DET-{n:06d}-{slug}.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"detection-strategy","id":f"DET-{n:06d}","name":name,"summary":summary,"description":description,"detects_refs":targets,"domains":["enterprise"],"analytic_refs":analytics,"evidence_refs":refs,"lifecycle":life()})
def analytic(n,slug,det,name,summary,platforms,logic,dr,obs,window,dims,fp,blind,tune,refs): write(f"analytics/NJA-{n:06d}-{slug}.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"detection-analytic","id":f"NJA-{n:06d}","strategy_ref":det,"name":name,"summary":summary,"domains":["enterprise"],"platforms":platforms,"logic":logic,"data_requirements":dr,"observables":obs,"correlation":{"window":window,"dimensions":dims},"false_positives":fp,"blind_spots":blind,"tuning_guidance":tune,"evidence_refs":refs,"lifecycle":life()})

strategy(230,"destination-capacity-source-topology",B("目的容量与来源拓扑关联","Destination Capacity and Source-Topology Correlation"),B("跨流量域连接目的容量、来源分布和无请求响应，识别低贡献多源或反射网络 DoS。","Join destination capacity, source distribution, and unmatched responses across traffic domains to identify low-contribution multi-source or reflected network DoS."),PP(("Strategy 以网络容量与合法通信失败为结果门，分别用聚合来源和无请求反射两个 Analytic。共享 IPFIX 与 IF-MIB 数据，但前者聚合真实来源 fan-in，后者验证 visible responder 与 victim 请求不匹配；协议字段不可通用替换。","The strategy uses network capacity and legitimate-communication failure as the outcome gate and separate aggregate-source and unmatched-reflection analytics. They share IPFIX and IF-MIB, while the former aggregates real-origin fan-in and the latter verifies visible responders unmatched to victim requests; protocol fields are not universally interchangeable.")),["NJT-0198","NJS-0198-001","NJS-0198-002"],["NJA-000287","NJA-000288"],["REF-000664","REF-000956","REF-000957","REF-000958","REF-000960","REF-000961","REF-000962"])
analytic(287,"multi-source-aggregate-saturation","DET-000230",B("多源汇聚与接口饱和分析","Multi-Source Aggregation and Interface Saturation Analytic"),B("输出每源低贡献但目的 fan-in、接口利用/丢弃和业务失败共同上升的网络洪泛。","Emit flooding where per-source contribution remains low while destination fan-in, interface utilization or discard, and business failures rise together."),["Network Devices"],PP(("把 IPFIX 按 destination、port/protocol、observationDomain 和 10/60 秒窗口聚合，计算来源 IP/AS 数、每源 octet/packet 分位、总量、SYN/UDP 比和 fan-in。与 IF-MIB ifHCInOctets/packets/discards/errors/ifHighSpeed 对齐，校正 samplingInterval 和 counter discontinuity。","Aggregate IPFIX by destination, port or protocol, observationDomain, and 10 or 60 second windows, calculating source IP or AS count, per-source octet or packet quantiles, totals, SYN or UDP ratios, and fan-in. Align IF-MIB octets, packets, discards, errors, and speed, correcting sampling and counter discontinuity."),("当总量/丢弃/时延接近容量且合法探针失败，而大多数来源低于单源基线时输出；在五分钟连接业务事件、CDN/发布和上游清洗结果。","Emit when totals, discard, or latency approach capacity and legitimate probes fail while most sources stay below per-source baseline; over five minutes join business events, CDN or releases, and upstream scrubbing.")),[req("ipfix-flow",B("IPFIX/NetFlow 流","IPFIX or NetFlow flows"),"IPFIX/NetFlow",["flow.start","flow.end","source.ip","destination.ip","source.port","destination.port","protocol","packet.count","octet.count","tcp.flags","ingress.interface","observation.domain","source.as","sampling.interval"]),req("interface-capacity",B("IF-MIB 接口容量","IF-MIB interface capacity"),"SNMP IF-MIB",["event.time","interface.id","in.octets","in.packets","in.discards","in.errors","high.speed","counter.discontinuity"]),req("network-service-health",B("网络服务健康与业务事件","Network service health and business events"),None,["event.time","destination.id","probe.success","latency","packet.loss","event.id","approval.id"])],[B("大量来源低贡献但目的 fan-in 和接口利用同步上升","Many low-contribution sources coincide with rising destination fan-in and interface utilization"),B("丢弃/错误与合法探针失败相交","Discard or errors intersect legitimate-probe failure")],B("10 秒、60 秒多尺度，业务/清洗关联五分钟，基线至少 30 天。","Use 10-second and 60-second scales, five minutes for business or scrubbing context, and at least a 30-day baseline."),["destination.ip","destination.port","protocol","observation.domain","source.as","interface.id","event.time"],[B("软件发布、直播/新闻 flash crowd、CDN 回源、灾难事件和批准压测","Software release, live or news flash crowd, CDN origin traffic, disaster event, and approved load test")],[B("采样丢弱流、NAT/代理合并来源、多 observationDomain 时钟偏差和上游不可见","Sampling drops weak flows, NAT or proxy merges sources, clock skew across domains, and upstream invisibility")],P("按目的服务和接口容量调优 fan-in/利用，维护活动日历与批准压测；不按来源数量 alone 告警，要求容量与健康结果。","Tune fan-in and utilization by destination service and interface capacity, maintain event calendars and approved tests, and never alert on source count alone without capacity and health outcome."),["REF-000664","REF-000956","REF-000957","REF-000961","REF-000962"])
analytic(288,"unmatched-reflected-response","DET-000230",B("无对应请求的反射响应关联","Unmatched Reflected-Response Correlation"),B("输出多第三方协议响应、无 victim 出站请求和容量损失构成的反射洪泛。","Emit reflected flooding formed by many third-party protocol replies, absent victim outbound requests, and capacity loss."),["Network Devices"],PP(("对 DNS/NTP/其他已建模协议，将入站响应与 victim 出站请求按事务 ID、五元组、时间和协议键在 30 秒匹配；统计 responder IP/AS、响应/请求包字节比、响应 fan-in 和无匹配比例。","For DNS, NTP, and other modeled protocols, match inbound replies to victim outbound requests by transaction ID, five-tuple, time, and protocol key over 30 seconds; calculate responder IP or AS count, response-to-request packet or byte ratio, response fan-in, and unmatched fraction."),("在 60 秒连接接口容量、丢弃与合法通信失败；只有协议响应语义、无请求和影响共同成立才输出。来源 validation 告警或 reflector reputation 仅作支持。","Within 60 seconds join interface capacity, discard, and legitimate-communication failure; emit only when protocol-response semantics, unmatched requests, and impact all hold. Source-validation alerts or reflector reputation are supporting evidence only.")),[req("bidirectional-protocol-flow",B("双向协议流与事务","Bidirectional protocol flows and transactions"),"IPFIX plus protocol telemetry",["event.time","direction","source.ip","destination.ip","source.port","destination.port","protocol","transaction.id","message.type","packet.length","octet.count"]),req("interface-capacity",B("接口容量与丢弃","Interface capacity and discard"),"SNMP IF-MIB",["event.time","interface.id","in.octets","in.discards","high.speed"]),req("network-service-health",B("网络健康结果","Network health outcomes"),None,["event.time","destination.id","probe.success","latency","packet.loss"])],[B("来自许多第三方的响应没有对应 victim 请求","Responses from many third parties have no matching victim requests"),B("响应 fan-in 与容量/丢弃和合法通信失败同步","Response fan-in coincides with capacity or discard and failed legitimate communication")],B("请求响应匹配 30 秒，容量/影响 60 秒；按协议往返时间调优。","Use 30 seconds for request-response matching and 60 seconds for capacity and impact, tuned to protocol RTT."),["destination.ip","protocol","transaction.id","source.as","interface.id","event.time"],[B("异步通知、DNS 递归/cache、Anycast、监测探针和合法大响应","Asynchronous notifications, DNS recursion or cache, Anycast, monitoring probes, and legitimate large responses")],[B("无 victim 出站日志、加密协议、NAT、采样或 transaction ID 缺失","Missing victim outbound logs, encrypted protocols, NAT, sampling, or absent transaction IDs")],P("为每个反射协议定义 request/response 键和正常放大范围，不用通用包长比覆盖所有协议；无请求判断降级时标记概率置信。","Define request and response keys and normal amplification range per protocol rather than one packet-size ratio; mark probabilistic confidence when unmatched-request evidence degrades."),["REF-000958","REF-000960","REF-000664","REF-000961"])

strategy(231,"external-input-endpoint-capacity",B("外部输入到端点容量与可用性","External Input to Endpoint Capacity and Availability"),B("连接入口请求、内部连接/工作/CPU 成本和独立健康，发现低流量状态保持或输入成本放大。","Join ingress requests, internal connection or worker or CPU cost, and independent health to detect low-traffic state holding or input-cost amplification."),PP(("Strategy 分开处理未完成状态积累和已完成输入的高内部代价。两者共享 availability 门，但第一个消费连接 progress/age 与池容量，第二个消费 route/input 与 per-request work/crash；高流量普通耗尽由父级聚合逻辑覆盖。","The strategy separates incomplete-state accumulation from high internal cost of completed inputs. Both share an availability gate, while the first consumes connection progress and age plus pool capacity and the second route and input plus per-request work or crash. Ordinary high-volume exhaustion is parent-level context.")),["NJT-0199","NJS-0199-001","NJS-0199-002"],["NJA-000289","NJA-000290"],["REF-000965","REF-000966","REF-000967","REF-000968","REF-000969","REF-000970","REF-000971","REF-000972","REF-000973","REF-000974","REF-000975"])
analytic(289,"state-holding-endpoint-exhaustion","DET-000231",B("状态保持连接与端点耗尽分析","State-Holding Connection and Endpoint Exhaustion Analytic"),B("输出低进度长连接积累、连接/worker 池饱和和合法健康失败。","Emit accumulating low-progress long connections, connection or worker-pool saturation, and failed legitimate health."),["Linux","Windows","macOS"],PP(("按 target/route 在 10 秒、60 秒和 5 分钟聚合 active/new/rejected connections、完成请求、processed bytes、408/503/504、connection age 和 byte progress。计算 active/completed、bytes/active 和超时率，并连接 worker/handle/queue 与外部探针。","Aggregate active, new, and rejected connections, completed requests, processed bytes, 408 or 503 or 504, connection age, and byte progress by target and route over 10 seconds, 60 seconds, and five minutes. Calculate active-to-completed, bytes per active connection, and timeout rate and join workers, handles, queues, and external probes."),("当 active/worker 接近上限、进度低而带宽/完成数不高、合法探针失败时输出；按 source 与全局两级分析，避免只用单源阈值。","Emit when active connections or workers approach limits, progress is low without high bandwidth or completions, and legitimate probes fail. Analyze per source and globally rather than using only source thresholds.")),[req("load-balancer-capacity",B("负载均衡容量指标","Load-balancer capacity metrics"),"ALB CloudWatch or equivalent",["event.time","target.id","active.connections","new.connections","rejected.connections","request.count","processed.bytes","http.4xx","http.5xx"]),req("request-progress-log",B("请求与连接进度","Request and connection progress"),"Web server and access logs",["event.time","connection.id","source.ip","route","request.length","bytes.received","connection.age","request.duration","status","error.type"]),req("endpoint-pool-health",B("端点池与业务健康","Endpoint pool and business health"),None,["event.time","service.id","workers.active","workers.max","queue.depth","handles.used","probe.success","latency"])],[B("active/completed 上升而 bytes 和请求完成率较低","Active-to-completed rises while bytes and completion rate remain low"),B("连接/worker 饱和与合法探针失败相交","Connection or worker saturation intersects legitimate-probe failure")],B("10 秒/60 秒/5 分钟多尺度，按 endpoint 超时调优。","Use 10-second, 60-second, and five-minute scales tuned to endpoint timeouts."),["service.id","target.id","route","connection.id","source.ip","event.time"],[B("慢移动客户端、大上传、长轮询、合法 WebSocket、流量峰值和后端延迟","Slow mobile clients, large uploads, long polling, legitimate WebSockets, traffic peaks, and backend delay")],[B("完成时才写日志、TLS/代理隐藏进度、连接 ID 不贯通或自定义服务器无池指标","Completion-only logs, TLS or proxy hiding progress, disconnected connection IDs, or custom servers without pool metrics")],P("按 route/客户端类型维护正常 progress 与连接寿命；保护合法慢客户端同时用阶段 timeout、最小 data rate 和全局并发门。严重度必须包含内部容量和健康失败。","Baseline progress and connection lifetime by route and client type; protect legitimate slow clients while applying stage timeouts, minimum data rates, and global concurrency gates. Severity requires internal capacity and health failure."),["REF-000965","REF-000966","REF-000967","REF-000971","REF-000972","REF-000973"])
analytic(290,"input-work-cost-amplification","DET-000231",B("输入到内部工作成本放大分析","Input-to-Internal-Work Cost Amplification Analytic"),B("输出少量/短请求与异常 route 时延、CPU/事件循环阻塞、错误或 crash 的不对称。","Emit asymmetry between a few or short requests and abnormal route duration, CPU or event-loop blocking, errors, or crash."),["Linux","Windows","macOS"],PP(("从 WAF/ALB/应用日志取得 request ID、source、method、URI、args、headers、request length、route、target、processing time、status、error 与 trace；按 trace/request 连接 OTel duration、应用 CPU/heap/event-loop lag、OOM/crash/restart 和外部健康。","Obtain request ID, source, method, URI, args, headers, request length, route, target, processing time, status, error, and trace from WAF, ALB, and application logs. Join by trace or request to OTel duration, application CPU, heap, event-loop lag, OOM, crash or restart, and external health."),("按 route 建 30 天输入长度—时延/资源基线，在 1 分钟和 15 分钟查找短输入/低请求数却异常高代价和健康失败。对重复结构做安全特征化，不在生产重放恶意 payload。","Build a 30-day input-length-to-duration or resource baseline per route and find short input or low request count with anomalously high cost and health failure over one and fifteen minutes. Safely characterize repeated structure without replaying malicious payloads in production.")),[req("waf-alb-request",B("WAF/ALB 请求与目标日志","WAF or ALB request and target logs"),"AWS WAF and ALB access logs",["event.time","request.id","trace.id","source.ip","http.method","uri","query.args","request.length","target.id","request.time","target.time","status","error.reason"]),req("otel-http",B("OpenTelemetry HTTP 指标与 trace","OpenTelemetry HTTP metrics and traces"),"OpenTelemetry",["event.time","trace.id","route","method","server.duration","status.code","error.type"]),req("application-resource-health",B("应用资源与可用性","Application resources and availability"),None,["event.time","process.id","cpu.time","memory.bytes","event.loop.lag","oom.event","crash.id","restart.id","probe.success"])],[B("短输入/低请求数对应异常 route 时延和资源代价","Short input or low request count maps to anomalous route duration and resource cost"),B("同一输入结构与 OOM/crash 或合法健康失败相连","The same input structure joins OOM or crash or legitimate-health failure")],B("请求到 trace 正负一分钟；route 成本 1/15 分钟；基线 30 天。","Use plus or minus one minute from request to trace, one or fifteen minutes for route cost, and a 30-day baseline."),["route","request.id","trace.id","source.ip","input.feature","process.id","event.time"],[B("合法复杂搜索/正则、报表生成、冷缓存、GC、部署回归和压测","Legitimate complex search or regex, report generation, cold cache, GC, deployment regression, and load test")],[B("无 per-request CPU、采样 trace、加密参数、异步队列断开 request ID 或 crash 后日志丢失","No per-request CPU, sampled traces, encrypted parameters, async queue breaking request IDs, or logs lost after crash")],P("按 route 和输入类别调优，不用一个时延阈值。严重度需输入结构重复、内部成本与 health result；标准 OTel 不提供 per-request CPU 时标记推断。","Tune by route and input class rather than one duration threshold. Severity needs repeated input structure, internal cost, and health result; mark inference when standard OTel lacks per-request CPU."),["REF-000968","REF-000969","REF-000970","REF-000973","REF-000974","REF-000975"])

strategy(232,"lifecycle-authority-outcome",B("生命周期控制权威至可用性结果谱系","Lifecycle Authority to Availability-Outcome Lineage"),B("连接本地请求者、未来任务或外部管理面动作到实际关机/重启和合法访问中断。","Join local requester, future task, or external management-plane action to actual shutdown or reboot and legitimate-access interruption."),PP(("Strategy 用三条 Analytic 分离 immediate local、deferred scheduler 和 external hypervisor/cloud 路径。确认门是攻击者控制 lifecycle action、实际 boot/power transition 和 availability 结果；reason、命令或 guest heartbeat alone 不确认。","The strategy uses three analytics for immediate local, deferred scheduler, and external hypervisor or cloud paths. Confirmation requires attacker-controlled lifecycle action, actual boot or power transition, and availability outcome; reason, command, or guest heartbeat alone does not confirm.")),["NJT-0200","NJS-0200-001","NJS-0200-002"],["NJA-000291","NJA-000292","NJA-000293"],["REF-000870","REF-000294","REF-000601","REF-000977","REF-000978","REF-000979","REF-000980","REF-000981","REF-000982","REF-000983"])
analytic(291,"local-request-lifecycle-outcome","DET-000232",B("本地关机请求者—生命周期结果分析","Local Shutdown Requester–Lifecycle Outcome Analytic"),B("输出本地进程/WMI 请求者、权限、reason、Event 1074 与后继 boot/可用性链。","Emit local process or WMI requester, authority, reason, Event 1074, and successor boot or availability chain."),["Windows"],PP(("连接 4688/DeviceProcessEvents 的 shutdown/restart process/command、ExitWindowsEx/WMI request attribution 和 Event 1074 requester/process/user/reason/type/comment；按 CorrelationId/OperationId 或进程/用户/时间匹配。","Join shutdown or restart process or command from 4688 or DeviceProcessEvents, ExitWindowsEx or WMI request attribution, and Event 1074 requester, process, user, reason, type, and comment by correlation or operation ID or process, user, and time."),("两分钟内验证 clean shutdown/start events 和 boot ID/uptime，三十分钟连接审批、维护窗口、外部 health 和用户影响。Event 41/6008 无受控请求先归 T1499/故障调查。","Within two minutes verify clean shutdown or start events and boot ID or uptime, and over thirty minutes join approval, maintenance window, external health, and user impact. Event 41 or 6008 without a controlled request routes first to T1499 or fault investigation.")),[req("windows-process-lifecycle",B("Windows 生命周期进程与 WMI","Windows lifecycle process and WMI"),"DeviceProcessEvents, Security, WMI tracing",["event.time","device.id","process.unique.id","process.name","process.command.line","account.sid","correlation.id","operation.id","client.machine","client.process.id"]),req("windows-system-lifecycle",B("Windows 系统生命周期事件","Windows system lifecycle events"),"System event log",["event.time","device.id","event.id","requester.process","requester.user","reason.code","shutdown.type","comment","boot.id","uptime"]),req("lifecycle-approval-health",B("生命周期审批与健康","Lifecycle approval and health"),None,["asset.id","approval.id","maintenance.window","probe.success","user.impact","owner.id"])],[B("无审批的 requester 与 Event 1074 及 clean transition 相连","An unapproved requester joins Event 1074 and a clean transition"),B("生命周期转换与外部健康/用户访问中断相交","Lifecycle transition intersects external health or user-access interruption")],B("requester 到 Event 1074 两分钟，审批/可用性三十分钟。","Use two minutes from requester to Event 1074 and thirty for approval and availability."),["device.id","process.unique.id","account.sid","correlation.id","boot.id","event.time"],[B("补丁、安装、故障恢复、管理员维护、UPS/电源策略和灾备","Patching, installation, fault recovery, administrator maintenance, UPS or power policy, and DR")],[B("硬断电、日志丢失、时钟变化、远程管理未记录或 requester 被代理进程遮蔽","Hard power loss, lost logs, clock change, unlogged remote management, or requester hidden by a broker process")],P("按资产角色维护允许 requester/reason/窗口与 owner；reason 不作为批准。无受控请求的 unexpected reboot 单独调查，避免把故障推成 T1529。","Baseline allowed requester, reason, window, and owner by asset role; a reason is not approval. Investigate unexpected reboot without controlled request separately rather than forcing T1529."),["REF-000294","REF-000977","REF-000978","REF-000979","REF-000980"])
analytic(292,"deferred-task-lifecycle-outcome","DET-000232",B("未来任务登记—调度执行—启动结果分析","Future Task Registration–Scheduled Execution–Boot Outcome Analytic"),B("输出关机/重启任务 writer、definition、runtime 和后来 boot 的长期谱系。","Emit long-lived lineage from shutdown or reboot task writer and definition through runtime and later boot."),["Windows"],PP(("采集 Task Scheduler Operational/Security 的注册、更新、删除、run instance 和 action，保存 task ID/path、definition digest、creator SID/process、runtime principal、scheduled/actual time、command/args、approval。","Collect Task Scheduler Operational or Security registration, update, deletion, run instance, and action, preserving task ID or path, definition digest, creator SID or process, runtime principal, scheduled and actual time, command or arguments, and approval."),("从登记保留到 scheduled time+15 分钟（初始 cap 24 小时），连接 scheduler child/shutdown process、Event 1074 在两分钟及 boot/outage 在三十分钟。重复 task ID 必须用 definition digest/run instance 区分。","Retain from registration through scheduled time plus 15 minutes, initially capped at 24 hours, and join scheduler child or shutdown process to Event 1074 within two minutes and boot or outage within thirty. Distinguish reused task IDs by definition digest and run instance.")),[req("scheduled-task-lifecycle",B("计划任务生命周期","Scheduled-task lifecycle"),"Task Scheduler Operational and Security",["event.time","asset.id","task.id","task.path","definition.digest","creator.sid","creator.process.id","runtime.principal","run.instance.id","scheduled.time","action.command","action.arguments","approval.id"]),req("windows-system-lifecycle",B("Windows 生命周期结果","Windows lifecycle outcome"),"System event log",["event.time","asset.id","event.id","requester.process","boot.id","uptime","shutdown.type"]),req("business-health",B("业务健康与 owner","Business health and owner"),None,["asset.id","owner.id","probe.success","user.impact","maintenance.window"])],[B("未来 shutdown/reboot action 由无审批 writer 登记并按计划执行","A future shutdown or reboot action is registered by an unapproved writer and executes on schedule"),B("scheduler runtime 与 boot/outage 在任务定义窗口闭合","Scheduler runtime and boot or outage close within the task-definition window")],B("登记到 scheduled+15 分钟，cap 24 小时；执行到 Event 1074 两分钟、boot 三十分钟。","Retain registration to scheduled plus 15 minutes, capped at 24 hours; two minutes to Event 1074 and thirty to boot."),["asset.id","task.id","definition.digest","creator.sid","runtime.principal","run.instance.id","scheduled.time","boot.id"],[B("补丁、安装、备份、维护、自动恢复和计划重启","Patching, install, backup, maintenance, automatic recovery, and scheduled restart")],[B("任务审计关闭、TaskCache 直接修改、task ID 重用、删除后未采、时钟篡改或 MDM provider-only 调度","Task audit disabled, direct TaskCache mutation, task ID reuse, deletion before collection, clock tampering, or provider-only MDM schedules")],P("对 shutdown/reboot action 要求 creator/runtime allowlist、definition digest、owner、审批和到期；不全局放行 SYSTEM。关键 task 生命周期保留 90 天。","Require creator and runtime allowlists, definition digest, owner, approval, and expiry for shutdown or reboot actions; never globally allow SYSTEM. Retain critical task lifecycle for 90 days."),["REF-000601","REF-000977","REF-000980"])
analytic(293,"management-plane-power-outcome","DET-000232",B("管理面电源动作—目标可用性结果分析","Management-Plane Power Action–Target Availability Analytic"),B("输出 hypervisor/cloud actor 和 power action 到 VM/设备离线与业务中断的跨平面链。","Emit cross-plane lineage from hypervisor or cloud actor and power action to VM or device offline and business interruption."),["ESXi","IaaS"],PP(("从 vSphere/cloud audit 采集 event key/chainId/auditId、createdTime、userName/principal、source、host、VM/target、power action、message、request ID 和 result；连接 session/role/approval 和资产 inventory。","Collect event key, chainId, auditId, time, user or principal, source, host, VM or target, power action, message, request ID, and result from vSphere or cloud audit and join session, role, approval, and asset inventory."),("在两分钟验证 target power state 和 guest heartbeat/网络消失，三十分钟连接业务 probe 与用户影响；后继 VMDK 加密另映射 NJT-0157。只有 host/网络失联而无成功 power event 不确认。","Within two minutes verify target power state and guest heartbeat or network disappearance and within thirty join business probe and user impact. Later VMDK encryption maps separately to NJT-0157. Host or network loss without a successful power event does not confirm.")),[req("management-power-event",B("虚拟化/云电源事件","Virtualization or cloud power events"),"vSphere Events or cloud audit",["event.time","event.key","chain.id","audit.id","principal.id","source.ip","host.id","target.id","power.action","request.id","result"]),req("target-power-state",B("目标电源与 heartbeat","Target power and heartbeat"),None,["event.time","target.id","host.id","power.state","guest.heartbeat","network.state","boot.id"]),req("business-health",B("业务健康与审批","Business health and approval"),None,["target.id","owner.id","approval.id","probe.success","user.impact"])],[B("未经批准主体从目标外控制面成功 power off/reboot","An unapproved principal successfully powers off or reboots from an out-of-target plane"),B("管理面结果与 guest heartbeat/业务可用性丢失闭合","Management outcome closes with lost guest heartbeat and business availability")],B("power event 到 target state 两分钟，业务影响三十分钟。","Use two minutes from power event to target state and thirty for business impact."),["principal.id","host.id","target.id","chain.id","audit.id","request.id","event.time"],[B("批准运维、HA/failover、DR、容量迁移、宿主维护和自动恢复","Approved operations, HA or failover, DR, capacity migration, host maintenance, and auto recovery")],[B("guest-only telemetry、控制面日志未保留、共享管理员、链 ID 丢失或 host crash 模拟 power off","Guest-only telemetry, absent control-plane retention, shared admins, lost chain IDs, or host crash resembling power off")],P("按 target class 限制 power roles，要求 JIT/MFA/审批并保留不可变审计；成功事件必须与实际 target state 匹配，不按 guest heartbeat alone 响应。","Limit power roles by target class, require JIT, MFA, and approval, and retain immutable audit. Match successful events to actual target state and never respond from guest heartbeat alone."),["REF-000981","REF-000982","REF-000983"])

strategy(233,"identity-removal-victim-denial",B("身份状态撤除到合法主体访问失败","Identity-State Removal to Legitimate-Principal Access Failure"),B("连接认证器或授权边的负向变化与合法 owner 登录/资源 deny，确认账户访问移除。","Join negative authenticator or authorization-edge mutations to legitimate-owner sign-in or resource denial to confirm Account Access Removal."),PP(("Strategy 使用认证器置换与授权边撤除两个 Analytic。两者共享 existing principal、未经批准 mutation 和 post-state failure 门；前者终态是认证失败，后者是认证成功但资源 deny，数据与恢复路径不可互换。","The strategy uses authenticator-displacement and authorization-edge eviction analytics. Both share existing principal, unapproved mutation, and post-state failure gates; the former ends at authentication failure and the latter at successful authentication plus resource denial, with non-interchangeable data and recovery.")),["NJT-0201","NJS-0201-001","NJS-0201-002"],["NJA-000294","NJA-000295"],["REF-000103","REF-000167","REF-000985","REF-000986","REF-000987","REF-000376"])
analytic(294,"authenticator-displacement-lockout","DET-000233",B("认证器置换到 owner 登录失败分析","Authenticator Displacement to Owner Sign-In Failure Analytic"),B("输出账户仍存在但 owner 方法被移除/替换并在后续登录失败的身份谱系。","Emit identity lineage where an account remains but owner methods are removed or replaced and later sign-in fails."),["SaaS"],PP(("从 Graph directoryAudit 识别密码重置、认证方法/SSPR/恢复属性移除与新增，保存 activityDateTime、initiatedBy、targetResources、category、operationType、result、correlationId、modifiedProperties old/new 和 approval。按 user/object 与 correlation 在 15 分钟聚合完整 method 差。","Identify password resets and authentication-method, SSPR, or recovery-property removals and additions from Graph directoryAudit, preserving time, initiator, targets, category, operation, result, correlation, modifiedProperties old and new, and approval. Aggregate the complete method differential by user or object and correlation over fifteen minutes."),("在三十分钟连接合法 owner signIn failure 的 user/resource/device/IP/status/error/risk/CA，与攻击者 method 登录/恢复结果；24 小时确认持续 lockout，90 天保留关键方法 lineage。方法 ID 缺失时降为主体级推断。","Within thirty minutes join legitimate-owner sign-in failure user, resource, device, IP, status, error, risk, and CA with attacker-method sign-in or recovery; confirm persistent lockout over 24 hours and retain critical method lineage for 90 days. Fall back to principal-level inference when method IDs are absent.")),[req("directory-audit",B("目录身份状态审计","Directory identity-state audit"),"Microsoft Graph directoryAudit",["event.time","initiator.id","target.id","activity.name","category","operation.type","result","correlation.id","property.name","value.old","value.new","approval.id"]),req("identity-signin",B("合法主体登录结果","Legitimate-principal sign-in outcomes"),"Microsoft Graph signIn",["event.time","user.id","resource.id","device.id","source.ip","status.code","failure.reason","risk.level","conditional.access.status","correlation.id"]),req("identity-owner-method",B("身份 owner 与方法清单","Identity owner and method inventory"),None,["user.id","owner.id","method.id","method.type","recovery.path","snapshot.time","breakglass.id"])],[B("账户保持启用但 owner 方法被移除/替换且 owner 登录失败","The account remains enabled while owner methods are removed or replaced and owner sign-in fails"),B("攻击者控制方法被新增并成功使用","An attacker-controlled method is added and successfully used")],B("mutation 聚合 15 分钟，owner failure 30 分钟，持续 lockout 24 小时，关键 lineage 90 天。","Aggregate mutations over 15 minutes, owner failure over 30, persistent lockout over 24 hours, and critical lineage over 90 days."),["user.id","initiator.id","method.id","correlation.id","resource.id","event.time"],[B("合法账户恢复、MFA 迁移、密码重置、fraud response、helpdesk 和设备更换","Legitimate account recovery, MFA migration, password reset, fraud response, helpdesk, and device replacement")],[B("signIn 无 method ID、审批系统被控制、owner 未尝试登录、离线/联合认证或日志留存短","Sign-in lacks method ID, compromised approval, owner makes no attempt, offline or federated authentication, or short retention")],P("要求 owner/工单/发起来源/方法寿命匹配，不对 helpdesk 或管理员全局放行。只有 mutation+owner failure 才确认，未测试保持风险。定期测试独立 break-glass。","Require matching owner, ticket, initiating origin, and method lifetime without globally allowing helpdesk or administrators. Confirm only mutation plus owner failure and keep untested cases as risk. Regularly test independent break-glass."),["REF-000167","REF-000985","REF-000986","REF-000987","REF-000376"])
analytic(295,"authorization-edge-eviction","DET-000233",B("授权图边撤除到资源拒绝分析","Authorization-Graph Edge Eviction to Resource Denial Analytic"),B("输出关键 role/group/delegation/owner 边被撤除并导致合法主体资源 deny 的谱系。","Emit lineage where a critical role, group, delegation, or owner edge is removed and causes resource denial for the legitimate principal."),["SaaS"],PP(("从 directoryAudit 和周期图快照识别角色/组/委托/owner/policy edge delete/update，保存 initiator、target、old/new、correlation、result 和 approval；按 tenant、principal、edge ID 在 30 分钟收敛 propagation。","Identify role, group, delegation, owner, or policy-edge delete or update from directoryAudit and graph snapshots, preserving initiator, target, old and new state, correlation, result, and approval; converge propagation by tenant, principal, and edge ID over thirty minutes."),("连接合法主体认证成功后资源访问 deny、缺失 role claims、owner/admin 操作失败与 break-glass 测试。24 小时内确认持续 access loss；边在变更前不存在或正常到期则不确认。","Join resource-access denial after successful authentication, missing role claims, failed owner or admin operation, and break-glass test. Confirm persistent access loss over 24 hours; do not confirm if the edge did not exist before or expired normally.")),[req("directory-audit",B("目录授权变更审计","Directory authorization-change audit"),"Microsoft Graph directoryAudit",["event.time","tenant.id","initiator.id","target.id","activity.name","operation.type","result","correlation.id","property.name","value.old","value.new","approval.id"]),req("authorization-graph",B("授权图前后快照","Authorization graph before and after snapshots"),None,["snapshot.time","tenant.id","principal.id","edge.id","edge.type","resource.id","valid.from","valid.to"]),req("resource-access-outcome",B("资源访问与 break-glass 结果","Resource access and break-glass outcomes"),None,["event.time","tenant.id","principal.id","resource.id","authentication.result","authorization.result","failure.reason","role.claims","breakglass.test.result"])],[B("关键授权边无审批撤除后合法主体认证成功但资源 deny","A critical edge is removed without approval and the legitimate principal authenticates but is denied"),B("owner/admin 操作失败且 break-glass/恢复路径不足","Owner or admin operations fail and break-glass or recovery is insufficient")],B("edge propagation 30 分钟，持续 loss 24 小时，关键图/审计保留 90 天。","Use 30 minutes for edge propagation, 24 hours for persistent loss, and 90 days for critical graph and audit retention."),["tenant.id","principal.id","edge.id","edge.type","resource.id","initiator.id","event.time"],[B("offboarding、PIM/JIT 到期、岗位调整、least privilege 清理、fraud response 和资源退役","Offboarding, PIM or JIT expiry, role change, least-privilege cleanup, fraud response, and resource retirement")],[B("图快照不完整、传播延迟、嵌套组、外部 IdP、资源日志缺失或审批被控制","Incomplete graph snapshots, propagation delay, nested groups, external IdP, absent resource logs, or compromised approval")],P("关键 owner/Global Admin/恢复边要求双人审批、PIM 和不可变审计；按 edge expiry 排除正常到期。确认需具体 edge-before、delete 和 resource deny，不用账户标签推断。","Require dual approval, PIM, and immutable audit for critical owner, Global Admin, and recovery edges; exclude normal expiry using edge validity. Confirmation needs a specific prior edge, deletion, and resource denial rather than account labels."),["REF-000103","REF-000985","REF-000986","REF-000987"])

analytic(296,"block-mutation-media-outcome","DET-000105",B("块设备破坏写入与介质结果分析","Block-Device Destructive Write and Media-Outcome Analytic"),B("输出 raw writer/driver、扇区范围、结构差和 mount/boot/数据集失败的闭合链。","Emit a closed chain of raw writer or driver, sector range, structural difference, and mount, boot, or dataset failure."),["Linux","Windows"],PP(("Linux 使用 audit raw block node open/write attribution、blkparse device/PID/command/RWBS/sector/length/time/error、block stats 和 lsblk before/after；Windows 需自建内核/raw-I/O sensor 提供 device/offset/length/operation/result，DeviceFileEvents 只补充工件，不能伪称有 sector。","On Linux use audit attribution for raw block-node open or write, blkparse device, PID, command, RWBS, sector, length, time, and error, block stats, and lsblk before and after. Windows requires a custom kernel or raw-I/O sensor for device, offset, length, operation, and result; DeviceFileEvents supplements artifacts and cannot be claimed to contain sectors."),("按 asset/device/writer 在 15 分钟聚合写/丢弃范围，与 MBR/GPT/filesystem metadata hash/CRC、partition inventory、mount/boot 和业务 dataset 结果连接。小关键写入与全盘 wipe 分级，失败 IOCTL 是企图。","Aggregate write or discard scope by asset, device, and writer over fifteen minutes and join MBR, GPT, or filesystem metadata hash or CRC, partition inventory, mount or boot, and business-dataset outcome. Grade small critical writes versus full-disk wipes; failed IOCTL remains attempt.")),[req("raw-block-audit",B("原始块设备访问审计","Raw block-device access audit"),"Linux audit or custom Windows kernel sensor",["event.time","asset.id","process.id","account.id","device.id","operation","sector.offset","block.count","byte.count","result","ioctl.code"]),req("block-trace",B("块 I/O trace 与统计","Block I/O traces and statistics"),"blkparse and block stats or equivalent",["event.time","device.id","process.id","command","rwbs","sector","length","error","writes.completed","discard.sectors"]),req("disk-structure-inventory",B("磁盘结构与完整性清单","Disk structure and integrity inventory"),"lsblk or storage inventory",["snapshot.time","asset.id","device.id","partition.id","filesystem.type","mount.point","metadata.hash","metadata.crc","bootable"]),req("media-availability",B("介质可用性结果","Media availability outcome"),None,["event.time","asset.id","device.id","mount.result","boot.result","dataset.result","probe.success","approval.id"])],[B("未经批准 raw writer 对关键区间或大范围块执行成功写/丢弃","An unapproved raw writer successfully writes or discards critical extents or broad blocks"),B("结构差与 mount/boot/业务数据集失败闭合","A structural difference closes with mount, boot, or business-dataset failure")],B("写入范围 15 分钟，重启/mount/结果 30 分钟，结构快照按关键资产持续保留。","Use 15 minutes for write scope and 30 for reboot, mount, or outcome, retaining structure snapshots for critical assets."),["asset.id","device.id","process.id","account.id","sector.offset","partition.id","event.time"],[B("批准格式化、镜像部署、分区迁移、secure decommission、磁盘修复和压测","Approved formatting, imaging, partition migration, secure decommission, disk repair, and testing")],[B("Windows 无 sector telemetry、存储控制器/设备内部 sanitize、主机日志随盘失效、加密/RAID 抽象或 snapshot 层不可见","Windows lacks sector telemetry, controller or device-internal sanitize, host logs fail with disk, encryption or RAID abstraction, or invisible snapshot layer")],P("按 exact device/asset、writer account、二进制/驱动签名、operation/IOCTL、sector scope 和工单调优；不全局放行签名分区工具。关键 extents 优先并外部流式收集。","Tune by exact device or asset, writer account, binary or driver signature, operation or IOCTL, sector scope, and ticket; never globally allow signed partition tools. Prioritize critical extents and stream externally."),["REF-000988","REF-000989","REF-000990","REF-000992","REF-000993","REF-000994","REF-000840","REF-000366","REF-000995","REF-000996"])

strategy(234,"presented-recoverability-disk-reality",B("呈现可恢复性与磁盘真实状态差分","Presented Recoverability versus Disk Reality"),B("比较勒索/解密呈现、key/ID 保存语义和真实块破坏，发现不可恢复擦除被错误分类。","Compare ransom or decryption presentation, key or ID retention semantics, and actual block destruction to detect irreversible wiping misclassified as recoverable."),PP(("Strategy 不因 ransom note alone 判定 wipe。Analytic 连接勒索工件、样本 key/IV/ID 生成与持久化、恢复函数可达性、raw block/metadata 差和安全恢复测试；呈现宣称可恢复而实际无材料/结构毁坏时确认子项。","The strategy never infers wiping from a ransom note alone. The analytic joins ransom artifacts, sample key, IV, or ID generation and retention, recovery-function reachability, raw block or metadata differences, and safe recovery tests; it confirms when presentation claims recoverability while actual materials are absent or structures destroyed.")),["NJT-0202","NJS-0202-002"],["NJA-000297"],["REF-000989","REF-000990","REF-000991","REF-000475"])
analytic(297,"wipe-recoverability-pretext-differential","DET-000234",B("擦除可恢复性话术与介质现实差分","Wipe Recoverability-Pretext and Media-Reality Differential"),B("输出勒索呈现、无可用 key/恢复路径和真实块/结构毁坏之间的矛盾。","Emit the contradiction among ransomware presentation, absent usable key or recovery path, and real block or structure destruction."),["Windows"],PP(("采集 DeviceFileEvents/process lineage 中 ransom note、扩展名、安装 ID、重启/锁屏工件和样本 hash，静态/动态分析 key/IV/ID 生成、保存/传输、恢复函数与目标盘。与此同时接入 raw block analytic 的 device、critical metadata、partition/mount/boot result。","Collect ransom note, extension, installation ID, reboot or lock-screen artifacts, sample hash, and process lineage from file or process telemetry, and statically or dynamically analyze key, IV, or ID generation, retention or transmission, recovery functions, and target disks. In parallel ingest device, critical metadata, partition, mount, and boot results from the raw-block analytic."),("在事件首 30 分钟判断呈现是否声称可支付/解密，在隔离副本上验证恢复材料可导出且函数能作用；缺 key/随机 ID/结构毁坏与可恢复承诺共同成立才输出。不得在原盘运行未验证 decryptor。","Within the first thirty minutes classify whether presentation claims payable decryption and validate on an isolated copy whether recovery material is derivable and the function works. Emit only when absent key or random ID or structural destruction conflicts with a recoverability promise. Never run unverified decryptors on original media.")),[req("ransom-artifact-lineage",B("勒索工件与进程谱系","Ransom artifacts and process lineage"),"DeviceFileEvents and process telemetry",["event.time","asset.id","process.id","file.path","file.hash","artifact.type","installation.id","extension","message.hash","sample.hash"]),req("recovery-material-analysis",B("恢复材料与代码分析","Recovery material and code analysis"),None,["sample.hash","key.generated","key.persisted","key.transmitted","iv.persisted","id.derivable","recovery.function.present","target.device"]),req("disk-reality",B("磁盘结构与恢复结果","Disk structure and recovery outcome"),None,["asset.id","device.id","metadata.hash.before","metadata.hash.after","partition.result","mount.result","boot.result","isolated.restore.result"])],[B("勒索/解密承诺存在但 key/ID 无法导出恢复材料","Ransom or decryption promise exists but key or ID cannot yield recovery material"),B("块/结构毁坏使安全恢复函数不可作用","Block or structure destruction makes safe recovery functions unusable")],B("工件、样本和磁盘状态首 30 分钟关联；安全恢复验证按事件响应时限记录。","Join artifacts, sample, and disk state in the first thirty minutes; record safe recovery validation under incident-response timing."),["asset.id","sample.hash","process.id","device.id","installation.id","event.time"],[B("合法演练 wiper、测试 ransomware、损坏样本、错误 key escrow 或暂时无法取得密钥","Authorized wiper exercise, ransomware test, broken sample, key-escrow error, or temporarily unavailable key")],[B("样本未取得、混淆阻止分析、key 在外部 C2、磁盘无法镜像或恢复函数有破坏副作用","Missing sample, obfuscation blocking analysis, key held by external C2, disk cannot be imaged, or recovery function has destructive side effects")],P("按证据等级报告：ransomware-like、疑似不可恢复、已确认 wipe。恢复验证使用隔离副本，保全原始盘；不以扩展名、note 或零填充模式 alone 判定。","Report evidence levels: ransomware-like, suspected irrecoverable, confirmed wipe. Validate on an isolated copy and preserve original media; never classify from extension, note, or zero-fill pattern alone."),["REF-000989","REF-000990","REF-000991","REF-000475"])

# Extend DET-000105 with destructive-write coverage while preserving its strategy identity.
det105_path=next((ROOT/"detections").glob("DET-000105-*.yaml"));det105=yaml.safe_load(det105_path.read_text())
for x in ["NJT-0202","NJS-0202-001"]:
 if x not in det105["detects_refs"]: det105["detects_refs"].append(x)
if "NJA-000296" not in det105["analytic_refs"]: det105["analytic_refs"].append("NJA-000296")
for x in ["REF-000988","REF-000989","REF-000990","REF-000992","REF-000993","REF-000994","REF-000840","REF-000366","REF-000995","REF-000996"]:
 if x not in det105["evidence_refs"]: det105["evidence_refs"].append(x)
det105["lifecycle"]["modified"]=TODAY;det105["lifecycle"]["version"]="0.3.0"
det105_path.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(det105,allow_unicode=True,sort_keys=False,width=112),encoding="utf-8")

def measure(k,n,d,t): return {"key":k,"name":n,"description":d,"control_type":t}
def app(target,use,effect,limits): return {"target_ref":target,"use":use,"expected_effect":effect,"limitations":limits}
write("mitigations/MIT-000205-source-validation-upstream-absorption.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"mitigation","id":"MIT-000205","name":B("源验证、反射面约束与上游吸收","Source Validation, Reflector Constraint, and Upstream Absorption"),"summary":B("阻止伪造源、限制可被反射的服务并在上游扩容/清洗汇聚洪泛，降低网络 DoS。","Prevent spoofed sources, constrain reflector services, and absorb or scrub aggregate floods upstream to reduce network DoS."),"description":PP(("该控制在来源、反射服务与目的上游三个位置降低攻击。边界执行 BCP38/源验证，递归/UDP 服务限制访问与响应，目标预置 Anycast/CDN/清洗和联络流程；容量与路由变化由不同权监控验证。","This control reduces attacks at source, reflector service, and destination upstream. Boundaries enforce BCP38 or source validation, recursive or UDP services restrict access and responses, and targets prearrange Anycast, CDN, scrubbing, and contacts; differently authorized monitoring verifies capacity and routing changes.")),"domains":["enterprise"],"measures":[measure("source-address-validation",B("源地址验证","Source-Address Validation"),P("在可控边界实施 ingress/egress source validation/uRPF 等，阻断不属于来源网络的伪造地址并监测丢弃。","Apply ingress or egress source validation or uRPF at controlled boundaries to block addresses not belonging to the source network and monitor drops."),"preventive"),measure("reflector-surface-hardening",B("反射服务面约束","Reflector-Service Surface Hardening"),P("限制开放递归/未授权 UDP 服务，应用 ACL、response rate limiting 和最小响应，修复可放大配置。","Restrict open recursion and unauthorized UDP services and apply ACLs, response-rate limiting, and minimal responses, fixing amplifier configurations."),"exposure-reduction"),measure("upstream-absorption-response",B("上游吸收与响应编排","Upstream Absorption and Response Orchestration"),P("按业务容量预置 Anycast/CDN/清洗、RTBH/FlowSpec 或 provider playbook，保留合法流量保护与撤销条件。","Prearrange Anycast, CDN, scrubbing, RTBH or FlowSpec, or provider playbooks by business capacity, preserving legitimate-traffic protection and rollback conditions."),"containment")],"applications":[app("NJT-0198",P("对关键前缀建立容量/业务基线和上游清洗入口，实施源验证与反射服务治理，并定期演练 provider 通知和业务保护。","Establish capacity and business baselines and upstream scrubbing for critical prefixes, deploy source validation and reflector governance, and exercise provider notification and business protection."),P("降低可用攻击流量、提高目标可吸收容量并缩短洪泛持续时间。","Reduce available attack traffic, increase absorbable capacity, and shorten flood duration."),P("源验证需要跨网络采用，Anycast/清洗有成本且可被更大攻击压倒，误触发会影响合法流量。","Source validation needs cross-network adoption, Anycast or scrubbing costs money and can be overwhelmed, and false activation can affect legitimate traffic.")),app("NJS-0198-001",P("使用目的级全局限额和清洗，不依赖单源限速；跨域聚合小贡献来源并保护已验证合法事件。","Use destination-level global limits and scrubbing rather than per-source limits alone; aggregate small contributors across domains while protecting verified legitimate events."),P("多源分散不能通过每源低速绕过总体容量门。","Distributed sources cannot bypass aggregate capacity gates through low per-source rates."),P("flash crowds 同形，过紧全局门会拒绝真实用户；跨域数据可能延迟。","Flash crowds are isomorphic, strict global gates can deny real users, and cross-domain data can be delayed.")),app("NJS-0198-002",P("实施 BCP38/源验证，关闭开放 reflector 并对 DNS/NTP 等应用 ACL/RRL；与 provider 共享反射协议指纹和无请求响应证据。","Implement BCP38 or source validation, close open reflectors, apply ACLs or RRL to DNS, NTP, and peers, and share reflection fingerprints and unmatched-response evidence with providers."),P("伪造受害源和可用 reflector 数量下降，第三方响应洪泛更快被归因和阻断。","Victim-source spoofing and available reflectors decline, and third-party response floods are attributed and blocked faster."),P("无法控制外部 reflector，部分协议需要公开 UDP；不完整全球部署仍允许反射。","External reflectors are outside control, some protocols need public UDP, and incomplete global deployment still permits reflection."))],"evidence_refs":["REF-000956","REF-000958","REF-000959","REF-000960","REF-000963"],"lifecycle":life()})

write("mitigations/MIT-000206-endpoint-work-admission-cost-bounds.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"mitigation","id":"MIT-000206","name":B("端点工作准入、成本界限与优雅降级","Endpoint Work Admission, Cost Bounds, and Graceful Degradation"),"summary":B("限制连接状态和每输入内部工作，将高代价路径隔离并在过载时优雅降级，降低端点 DoS。","Bound connection state and per-input internal work, isolate expensive paths, and degrade gracefully under overload to reduce endpoint DoS."),"description":PP(("该控制同时治理会话持有与算法工作。前置代理和服务应用阶段 timeout、最小数据率、并发/队列限额；代码使用线性/非回溯算法、输入长度/复杂度与执行预算；高代价路径隔离到受限 worker，并用独立健康和 failover 避免级联。","This control governs both session holding and algorithmic work. Proxies and services apply stage timeouts, minimum data rates, concurrency and queue limits. Code uses linear or nonbacktracking algorithms, input length or complexity and execution budgets. Expensive paths are isolated in bounded workers, while independent health and failover prevent cascades.")),"domains":["enterprise"],"measures":[measure("connection-progress-bounds",B("连接进度与并发界限","Connection Progress and Concurrency Bounds"),P("按请求阶段设置 timeout/min-rate、每来源与全局并发、header/body/keepalive 界限，并保留慢合法客户端例外。","Set stage timeouts and minimum rates, per-source and global concurrency, and header, body, and keepalive bounds while preserving exceptions for slow legitimate clients."),"preventive"),measure("input-work-bounds",B("输入与内部工作成本界限","Input and Internal-Work Cost Bounds"),P("使用非回溯算法、输入长度/嵌套/复杂度限制、执行超时和 circuit breaker，在上线前复杂度测试。","Use nonbacktracking algorithms, input length, nesting and complexity limits, execution timeouts, and circuit breakers, testing complexity before release."),"preventive"),measure("isolated-graceful-degradation",B("隔离工作池与优雅降级","Isolated Worker Pools and Graceful Degradation"),P("为高代价 route 使用有界池/队列、backpressure、缓存和 failover，在过载时保留关键功能与独立健康。","Use bounded pools and queues, backpressure, caching, and failover for expensive routes and preserve critical function and independent health during overload."),"containment")],"applications":[app("NJT-0199",P("为关键 endpoint 建立资源/健康 SLO、入口准入和内部成本上限，隔离昂贵路径并演练过载/failover。","Establish resource and health SLOs, ingress admission, and internal-cost limits for critical endpoints, isolate expensive paths, and exercise overload and failover."),P("高量、低速和小输入高成本路径都更难耗尽共同资源，影响范围和持续时间下降。","High-volume, low-rate, and small-input high-cost paths have less ability to exhaust shared resources, reducing scope and duration."),P("严格限额会拒绝慢客户端或复杂合法任务，failover 可能同步过载；代码缺陷仍可能绕过通用门。","Strict limits can reject slow clients or complex legitimate tasks, failover can overload in parallel, and code flaws can bypass generic gates.")),app("NJS-0199-001",P("针对 header/body/keepalive 和连接池设置阶段 timeout、min-rate、全局并发与 progress 检查，不只按源 IP。","Set stage timeouts, minimum rate, global concurrency, and progress checks for headers, bodies, keepalive, and pools rather than source IP alone."),P("低速连接不能无限占用状态，多源低速也受全局门限制。","Slow connections cannot hold state indefinitely and distributed slow sources face global gates."),P("卫星/移动/大上传和长轮询需精确例外，攻击者可围绕门槛调速。","Satellite or mobile clients, large uploads, and long polling need precise exceptions, and attackers can pace around thresholds.")),app("NJS-0199-002",P("替换灾难性回溯正则、限制输入长度/嵌套、设置 per-route execution budget，并隔离 parser/报告 worker。","Replace catastrophic-backtracking regex, bound input length and nesting, set per-route execution budgets, and isolate parser or report workers."),P("小输入无法无限放大内部工作，单路由故障不再阻塞共享事件循环。","Small inputs cannot amplify work without bound and one route no longer blocks the shared event loop."),P("复杂度难静态预测，timeout 可中断合法重任务，原生库/内核路径可能不受应用预算控制。","Complexity is hard to predict statically, timeouts can interrupt legitimate heavy work, and native library or kernel paths may escape app budgets."))],"evidence_refs":["REF-000965","REF-000966","REF-000967","REF-000968","REF-000969","REF-000970"],"lifecycle":life()})

write("mitigations/MIT-000207-system-lifecycle-authority-resilience.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"mitigation","id":"MIT-000207","name":B("系统生命周期权限与可用性韧性","System Lifecycle Authority and Availability Resilience"),"summary":B("限制本地、调度与外部管理面的关机/重启权限，并以审批、不可变审计和高可用降低恶意生命周期影响。","Restrict shutdown and reboot authority across local, scheduled, and external management planes and reduce malicious lifecycle impact through approval, immutable audit, and availability resilience."),"description":PP(("此控制把生命周期 action 视为高影响事务。最小化 SeShutdown/remote power/hypervisor 权限，对关键系统要求 JIT、MFA、双人审批和不同权日志；未来任务需绑定 writer/definition/runtime/target/expiry；关键服务采用 HA 与经过演练的重启恢复。","This control treats lifecycle actions as high-impact transactions. Minimize local shutdown, remote power, and hypervisor rights, require JIT, MFA, dual approval, and differently authorized logs for critical systems, bind future tasks to writer, definition, runtime, target, and expiry, and use HA and exercised reboot recovery.")),"domains":["enterprise"],"measures":[measure("least-lifecycle-authority",B("最小生命周期权限","Least Lifecycle Authority"),P("限制本地/远程关机、云/虚拟化 power actions 和批量目标范围，关键操作使用短期身份、MFA 与双人审批。","Restrict local or remote shutdown, cloud or virtualization power actions, and bulk target scope and use short-lived identities, MFA, and dual approval for critical actions."),"preventive"),measure("future-action-governance",B("未来生命周期任务治理","Future Lifecycle-Task Governance"),P("对 shutdown/reboot task 记录 writer、definition digest、runtime、next run、target、approval 与 expiry，并在触发前撤销异常。","Record writer, definition digest, runtime, next run, target, approval, and expiry for shutdown or reboot tasks and revoke anomalies before triggering."),"preventive"),measure("external-audit-ha-recovery",B("外部审计、高可用与恢复","External Audit, High Availability, and Recovery"),P("在目标外保留 lifecycle audit/health，使用集群/HA、自动恢复与启动验证，并演练恶意重启后的业务一致性。","Retain lifecycle audit and health outside the target, use cluster or HA, automated recovery, and boot validation, and exercise business consistency after malicious reboot."),"containment")],"applications":[app("NJT-0200",P("对主机、VM 和设备 lifecycle 权限执行最小化与审批，将本地、任务和管理面事件统一到资产 owner 与外部健康，并演练 HA/recovery。","Apply least privilege and approval to host, VM, and device lifecycle authority, unify local, task, and management-plane events with asset owner and external health, and exercise HA and recovery."),P("未经批准关机/重启更难完成，actor 保持可追溯，业务中断时间缩短。","Unapproved shutdown or reboot becomes harder, actor remains attributable, and business interruption shortens."),P("紧急维护/故障恢复需相同权限，HA 可能共同受管理面攻击，重启本身仍会造成短时中断。","Emergency maintenance and fault recovery need the same rights, HA can share a compromised management plane, and reboot still causes transient interruption.")),app("NJS-0200-001",P("限制可创建 shutdown/reboot action 的 task writer/runtime，绑定 definition、creator、next-run、target、approval 与 boot，并在未来触发前阻断异常。","Restrict task writers and runtimes for shutdown or reboot actions, bind definition, creator, next run, target, approval, and boot, and block anomalies before future trigger."),P("关闭 writer 与结果的时间断点，调度器身份不再掩盖原始决定。","Close the temporal break between writer and outcome so scheduler identity no longer obscures the decision."),P("合法补丁高度依赖任务，时钟/离线补跑改变时间，受管 controller 受陷仍可满足策略。","Legitimate patching relies heavily on tasks, clock or offline catch-up changes time, and a compromised managed controller can satisfy policy.")),app("NJS-0200-002",P("分离 hypervisor/cloud power roles 与 guest admins，要求 JIT/MFA/审批，保留 vSphere/cloud immutable event，并限制批量 power scope。","Separate hypervisor or cloud power roles from guest admins, require JIT, MFA, and approval, retain immutable vSphere or cloud events, and limit bulk power scope."),P("guest 外动作可被目标外日志及时识别和撤销，单个管理身份不能静默关闭整个 fleet。","Out-of-guest actions are identified and revoked from external logs and one identity cannot silently power off an entire fleet."),P("控制面整体受陷、break-glass 滥用或 provider 日志延迟仍可能造成 fleet 中断。","Whole control-plane compromise, break-glass abuse, or delayed provider logs can still cause fleet outage."))],"evidence_refs":["REF-000977","REF-000978","REF-000979","REF-000980","REF-000981","REF-000983"],"lifecycle":life()})

write("mitigations/MIT-000208-wipe-impact-validation-response.yaml",{"schema_version":"2.0.0","type":"mitigation","id":"MIT-000208","name":B("擦除影响验证与证据保全响应","Wipe-Impact Validation and Evidence-Preserving Response"),"summary":B("快速验证介质结构和恢复材料，保全原盘并选择裸机恢复而非被虚假勒索话术误导。","Rapidly validate media structure and recovery material, preserve original disks, and choose bare-metal recovery rather than follow false ransom claims."),"description":PP(("此控制面向被伪装成可解密勒索的 disk wipe。事件响应先隔离写入者和设备，镜像/保全原盘，验证 MBR/GPT/filesystem 与 key/IV/ID 来源及恢复代码，再按证据选择解密、结构修复或裸机重建。未经验证的 decryptor 不在原盘运行。","This control addresses disk wipes presented as decryptable ransomware. Response isolates writer and device, images and preserves original media, validates MBR, GPT, filesystem, key or IV or ID provenance, and recovery code, then selects decryption, structure repair, or bare-metal rebuild by evidence. Unverified decryptors never run on original media.")),"domains":["enterprise"],"measures":[measure("preserve-validate-media",B("保全并验证介质状态","Preserve and Validate Media State"),P("停止写入、捕获 raw image 与关键 metadata，记录驱动/IOCTL/进程和块差，在隔离副本验证恢复。","Stop writes, capture raw images and critical metadata, record driver, IOCTL, process, and block differences, and validate recovery on isolated copies."),"containment"),measure("verify-recovery-material",B("验证 key、ID 与恢复代码","Verify Key, ID, and Recovery Code"),P("分析 key/IV/安装 ID 的生成、保存与传输以及恢复函数，按 ransomware-like、疑似 wipe、确认 wipe 分级。","Analyze key, IV, or installation-ID generation, retention, transmission, and recovery functions and grade ransomware-like, suspected wipe, and confirmed wipe."),"detective-support"),measure("bare-metal-recovery-playbook",B("裸机恢复与沟通预案","Bare-Metal Recovery and Communications Playbook"),P("维护独立裸机映像、partition maps、boot/config 与数据副本，演练重建并准备不可恢复事件的业务/法律沟通。","Maintain independent bare-metal images, partition maps, boot or configuration, and data copies, exercise rebuild, and prepare business and legal communications for irrecoverable incidents."),"containment")],"applications":[app("NJS-0202-002",P("在出现 ransom note/ID 时同时验证真实块结构和 key/recovery 语义，保全原盘，在隔离副本测试并在确认 wipe 后切换裸机重建。","When ransom notes or IDs appear, validate actual block structure and key or recovery semantics, preserve original media, test on isolated copies, and switch to bare-metal rebuild after confirmed wipe."),P("减少支付/错误解密造成的延迟和二次损伤，快速选择与真实介质状态匹配的响应。","Reduce delay and secondary damage from payment or incorrect decryption and rapidly choose a response matching media reality."),P("样本/密钥可能暂时不可得，完整镜像耗时，过早分类可能放弃可恢复数据；裸机恢复依赖镜像时效和外部副本。","Samples or keys may be temporarily unavailable, full imaging takes time, premature classification can abandon recoverable data, and bare-metal recovery depends on image freshness and external copies.")),app("NJT-0202",P("为 disk wipe 响应预置写入隔离、raw imaging、关键 metadata 快照、独立裸机映像与外部日志，按块结果而非工具/字条决定恢复路径。","Prearrange write isolation, raw imaging, critical-metadata snapshots, independent bare-metal images, and external logs for disk-wipe response and choose recovery by block outcome rather than tool or ransom note."),P("擦除影响被快速确认，介质证据和独立恢复路径存活，恢复范围更准确。","Wipe impact is confirmed quickly, media evidence and independent recovery survive, and restoration scope is more accurate."),P("该措施主要降低响应错误和恢复损失，不能阻止已获 raw-write 权限的攻击者；镜像和演练有成本。","The measure mainly reduces response error and recovery loss and cannot stop an actor already holding raw-write authority; imaging and exercises are costly."))],"evidence_refs":["REF-000988","REF-000989","REF-000990","REF-000991","REF-000995","REF-000996"],"lifecycle":life()})

# Extend existing controls with semantically identical target applications.
def extend_mit(mid,refs,apps,version):
 p=next((ROOT/"mitigations").glob(f"{mid}-*.yaml"));d=yaml.safe_load(p.read_text());existing={a["target_ref"] for a in d["applications"]};d["applications"].extend(a for a in apps if a["target_ref"] not in existing);d["evidence_refs"]=list(dict.fromkeys(d["evidence_refs"]+refs));d["lifecycle"]["modified"]=TODAY;d["lifecycle"]["version"]=version;p.write_text(yaml.safe_dump(d,allow_unicode=True,sort_keys=False,width=112),encoding="utf-8")
extend_mit("MIT-000088",["REF-000601","REF-000977","REF-000980"],[app("NJS-0200-001",P("对 shutdown/reboot task 限制 writer/runtime，保存 definition digest、creator、next run、target 与 approval，并在未来触发前撤销异常。","Restrict writers and runtimes for shutdown or reboot tasks, retain definition digest, creator, next run, target, and approval, and revoke anomalies before future trigger."),P("调度对象控制与长期保留关闭 writer 到结果的时间断点。","Scheduler-object control and long retention close the temporal break from writer to outcome."),P("合法补丁/安装/恢复使用相同调度器，审计缺口、后端直接修改和受陷 controller 仍会绕过。","Legitimate patching, installation, and recovery use the same scheduler, while audit gaps, direct backend mutation, and compromised controllers bypass it."))],"0.3.0")
extend_mit("MIT-000063",["REF-000103","REF-000167","REF-000985","REF-000986","REF-000987"],[app("NJT-0201",P("限制负向身份状态写权限，保存 old/new 与可恢复值，监控 owner post-state，并维护至少两个独立 break-glass 账户与完整恢复演练。","Restrict negative identity-state write authority, retain old and new and recoverable values, monitor owner post-state, and maintain at least two independent break-glass accounts with full recovery exercises."),P("认证器/授权边被恶意移除时可快速识别、回滚并恢复合法 owner 访问。","Malicious authenticator or authorization-edge removal is rapidly identified, rolled back, and legitimate-owner access restored."),P("审批或 break-glass 同时受陷、外部 IdP 或本地状态未采集时仍可能 tenant lockout。","Concurrent compromise of approval or break-glass, external IdP, or uncollected local state can still cause tenant lockout.")),app("NJS-0201-001",P("对密码/SSPR/MFA/恢复方法删除与新增实施强审批、owner 带外通知和 old-value/方法清单保留，测试独立恢复账户。","Apply strong approval, out-of-band owner notification, and old-value or method inventory retention to password, SSPR, MFA, and recovery-method deletion or addition and test independent recovery accounts."),P("排他认证器置换更难静默完成，owner 路径可恢复。","Exclusive authenticator displacement becomes harder to complete silently and owner paths remain recoverable."),P("某些密码不可恢复、紧急恢复本身可被社会工程，method ID 不完整会延迟定位。","Some passwords cannot be restored, emergency recovery can be socially engineered, and incomplete method IDs delay localization.")),app("NJS-0201-002",P("对 owner/Global Admin/组/角色/委托/policy edge 撤除使用 PIM/JIT、双人审批、graph snapshot 和资源级 break-glass 测试。","Use PIM or JIT, dual approval, graph snapshots, and resource-level break-glass testing for removal of owners, Global Admins, groups, roles, delegations, or policy edges."),P("授权边可回滚，认证成功但资源 deny 的锁定被快速发现并恢复。","Authorization edges are recoverable and lockout with successful authentication but resource denial is rapidly found and restored."),P("嵌套/外部图、传播延迟和审批系统受陷仍会隐藏真实有效边。","Nested or external graphs, propagation delay, and compromised approval can still hide effective edges."))],"1.1.0")
extend_mit("MIT-000107",["REF-000988","REF-000989","REF-000990","REF-000992","REF-000995","REF-000996"],[app("NJT-0202",P("限制 raw device/volume write、危险 IOCTL 和驱动加载到批准工具/身份/设备范围，监测关键 extents 并外部保留日志。","Restrict raw device or volume writes, dangerous IOCTLs, and driver load to approved tools, identities, and device scope, monitor critical extents, and retain logs externally."),P("攻击者更难取得或滥用 raw-write 权限，破坏写入在介质失效前可被阻断或归因。","Attackers have less ability to obtain or abuse raw-write rights and destructive writes can be blocked or attributed before media failure."),P("高权内核/存储控制器和签名但脆弱驱动可绕过，严格控制会影响运维/取证。","High-privilege kernels or storage controllers and signed vulnerable drivers can bypass controls, while strict controls affect operations and forensics.")),app("NJS-0202-001",P("对 MBR/GPT/MFT 等关键区间实施优先 raw-I/O 监测和结构 hash/CRC，任何无工单小范围写入立即阻断/隔离。","Prioritize raw-I/O monitoring and structure hash or CRC for MBR, GPT, MFT, and similar critical extents and block or isolate small writes without a ticket."),P("少量关键写入不再因总写量低而被忽略。","Small critical writes are no longer ignored because total volume is low."),P("结构随正常格式化/升级变化，跨文件系统 extent 清单和性能成本需管理。","Structures change during normal format or upgrade and cross-filesystem extent inventory and performance cost need management."))],"0.3.0")
extend_mit("MIT-000158",["REF-000988","REF-000990","REF-000995","REF-000996"],[app("NJT-0202",P("在生产盘 writer 权限之外保留裸机映像、partition maps、boot/config 和业务数据副本，并演练整盘/卷恢复。","Keep bare-metal images, partition maps, boot or configuration, and business-data copies outside production-disk writer authority and exercise full disk or volume restoration."),P("disk wipe 不会消除所有恢复路径，恢复同时验证结构与文件。","Disk wipe does not eliminate every recovery path and restoration validates structures as well as files."),P("同账户/controller snapshot 不独立，陈旧映像损失 RPO，备份不能阻止当前中断。","Snapshots in the same account or controller are not independent, stale images lose RPO, and backup cannot prevent current outage."))],"0.5.0")

extend_mit("MIT-000158",["REF-000988","REF-000989","REF-000995","REF-000996"],[app("NJS-0202-001",P("为关键元数据最小写入毁坏保留受不同权保护的 partition maps、boot/metadata 快照和裸机映像，并验证整卷重建。","For critical-metadata minimal-write destruction, keep differently authorized partition maps, boot or metadata snapshots, and bare-metal images and validate full-volume rebuild."),P("即使少量结构块被破坏，已知结构和独立映像仍可重建启动与文件系统。","Even when a few structural blocks are destroyed, known structures and independent images can rebuild boot and filesystem."),P("快照过旧、同控制面副本或结构记录不完整会降低恢复，且恢复不能阻止当前停机。","Stale snapshots, same-plane copies, or incomplete structure records weaken recovery, and restoration cannot prevent current outage."))],"0.5.0")

